{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019UUXX5Lib4nihYRLXeE3X3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '2-axis framework（connector coupling × task complexity）在所有 model×suite\n2\t  组合中得到干净验证。 CV diagnostic 形成完整的连续预测谱（0.038→0.314），scaling law 在 k=0.5 和 k=0.7 均成立且无例外。\n3\t  π0.5 uniformly critical 行为（L2norm 高原 + random cliff）泛化至 Spatial/Goal/Long，机制一致。\n4\t  VTR connector-dependency（pixel-shuffle 有效、MLP 失败）是干净且可解释的结果。 E5 attention pruning\n5\t  在 Goal suite 上完美泛化（SR=96.8-98.2%），为 entangling connector 提供 \"correct importance\n6\t  metric rescues\" 叙事。5 claims 全部保留，reviewer concern RC7 被 4 suites 完全化解。 Paper title\n7\t  不变。叙事核心：Analysis（primary）+ Diagnose-then-Compress method（secondary）。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: VTR M-sweep tri-seed completion (SmolVLA)\n12\t  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n13\t  description: 'SmolVLA VTR cross-attention M=16/32/64/96/128 全部 3-seed 完成。 MLP adapter\n14\t    M=32 3-seed 完成。M-curve 平坦性、架构独立性、near-lossless compression 已确认。 剩余工作：最终统计汇总与 paper\n15\t    table 生成。\n16\t\n17\t    '\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    m16_3seed_mean_sr: 56.9\n20\t    m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n21\t    m32_3seed_mean_sr: 60.1\n22\t    m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n23\t    m64_3seed_mean_sr: 62.0\n24\t    m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n25\t    m96_3seed_mean_sr: 54.5\n26\t    m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n27\t    m128_3seed_mean_sr: 58.0\n28\t    m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n29\t    mlp_adapter_m32_mean_sr: 63.4\n30\t    mlp_adapter_m32_std: 2.6\n31\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_m128: 0.98\n32\t    m_curve_max_range_pp: 7.5\n33\t    vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n34\t    baseline_sr: 59.2\n35\t  result_rationale: 'M-curve 平坦的根本原因：pixel-shuffle 的空间折叠创造了可逆的 token 纠缠。VTR 的 cross-attention\n36\t    学习了\"展开\"这种纠缠的映射——无论压缩到多少 query token（M=16→128），只要保留足够的 capacity 来表示空间结构，re-encoding\n37\t    就能恢复。M=128 passthrough（58.0%）≈baseline（59.2%）证明 VTR 是恢复而非增强。MLP adapter 与 cross-attention\n38\t    无显著差异（p=0.15）证明任何 learned  re-encoding 都能完成此恢复，不依赖特定架构机制。M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）是统计真实但\n39\t    实际影响有限的波动（54.5% 仍远高于 0% hard pruning）。\n40\t\n41\t    '\n42\t  tables:\n43\t  - title: 'Table: SmolVLA VTR M-sweep (3-seed)'\n44\t    columns:\n45\t    - M\n46\t    - Compression\n47\t    - SR mean±std (%)\n48\t    - vs Baseline Δ (pp)\n49\t    - p vs M=128\n50\t    data:\n51\t    - - '16'\n52\t      - 87.5%\n53\t      - 56.9±1.3\n54\t      - '-2.3'\n55\t      - '>0.25'\n56\t    - - '32'\n57\t      - 75%\n58\t      - 60.1±1.3\n59\t      - '+0.9'\n60\t      - '>0.25'\n61\t    - - '64'\n62\t      - 50%\n63\t      - 62.0±2.3\n64\t      - '+2.8'\n65\t      - '>0.25'\n66\t    - - '96'\n67\t      - 25%\n68\t      - 54.5±3.2\n69\t      - '-4.7'\n70\t      - 0.034*\n71\t    - - '128'\n72\t      - 0% (passthrough)\n73\t      - 58.0±3.5\n74\t      - '-1.2'\n75\t      - —\n76\t    - - MLP-adapter@32\n77\t      - 75%\n78\t      - 63.4±2.6\n79\t      - '+4.2'\n80\t      - —\n81\t    - - Hard pruning k=0.5\n82\t      - 50%\n83\t      - '0.0'\n84\t      - '-59.2'\n85\t      - —\n86\t  figures_description:\n87\t  - 'Fig: M-curve flat plot — x=M (16→128), y=SR(%). Horizontal band at baseline 59.2%±5pp,\n88\t    all M values within band. Hard pruning 0% shown as contrast.'\n89\t  analysis: 'VTR 在 pixel-shuffle connector 上实现 near-lossless compression at ANY ratio（0-87.5%）。\n90\t    这是 Claim 4 的核心证据。M=16 87.5% compression 仅损失 2.3pp，而 hard pruning 在 5% removal  即\n91\t    collapse 至 0%。recovery ratio 0.98 落在 best tier 目标范围 [0.95, 1.05] 内。 架构独立性（VTC\n92\t    vs MLP p=0.15）排除了特定机制假说，支持\"任何 learned re-encoding 均可修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement\"的一般性结论。\n93\t\n94\t    '\n95\t- name: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — connector-dependent ceiling\n96\t  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n97\t  description: 'VTR M=128 full training 已确认 0% SR（overfitting, 每步输出相同 action）。 VTC-only\n98\t    M=32/M=64 作为 fallback 继续训练。预测结果为 clean negative： VTR 对 MLP projector 无效，VTR ceiling\n99\t    取决于 connector 类型。\n100\t\n101\t    '\n102\t  expected_results:\n103\t    vtconly_m32_sr: 0.0\n104\t    vtconly_m64_sr: 0.0\n105\t    vtconly_m96_sr: 0.0\n106\t    vtr_m128_sr: 0.0\n107\t    openvla_baseline_sr: 74.0\n108\t    failure_mode: overfitting — model outputs identical action per step\n109\t    connector_dependency_confirmed: true\n110\t  result_rationale: 'MLP projector tokens 已经是独立且有意义的（CV=0.215，信息分布在 token 间有分化）。 VTR\n111\t    的 cross-attention 试图将这些已经 well-structured 的 token 重新编码为更少的 query  token，但这个重新编码过程引入了不必要的复杂性。MLP\n112\t    token 的信息是 per-token 局部化的， 与 pixel-shuffle token 的空间纠缠不同——后者的信息恢复 requires 全局\n113\t    re-arrangement， 恰好是 VTR cross-attention 擅长的。对 MLP projector，简单的 hard pruning（k=0.5\n114\t    仍有  37.4% SR）比 VTR 更有效，因为保留的 token 仍然 individually meaningful。VTR 的 22M  额外参数在缺乏\n115\t    spatial entanglement repair 目标时退化为纯噪声拟合器。 所有 M 值（32/64/96/128）均失败进一步证明这不是超参数问题而是架构兼容性问题。\n116\t\n117\t    '\n118\t  tables:\n119\t  - title: 'Table: VTR connector-dependency summary'\n120\t    columns:\n121\t    - Connector\n122\t    - Model\n123\t    - CV\n124\t    - Hard prune k=0.5 SR(%)\n125\t    - VTR M=32 SR(%)\n126\t    - VTR Δ vs prune (pp)\n127\t    data:\n128\t    - - Pixel-shuffle\n129\t      - SmolVLA\n130\t      - '0.314'\n131\t      - '0.0'\n132\t      - '60.1'\n133\t      - '+60.1'\n134\t    - - MLP (3-layer)\n135\t      - OpenVLA\n136\t      - '0.215'\n137\t      - '37.4'\n138\t      - '0.0'\n139\t      - '-37.4'\n140\t    - - Linear+BART\n141\t      - X-VLA\n142\t      - '0.151'\n143\t      - 42.6(L2)/70.6(R)\n144\t      - N/A\n145\t      - —\n146\t  figures_description:\n147\t  - 'Fig: VTR recovery diagram — SmolVLA: 0%→60% (recovery), OpenVLA: 37%→0% (degradation).\n148\t    Visual contrast showing connector-dependent VTR ceiling.'\n149\t  analysis: 'Clean negative result 强化了 paper narrative：VTR 是 pixel-shuffle 的特解而非通用压缩方法。\n150\t    这从 weakness 变为 strength——说明 Diagnose-then-Compress framework 的第一步（CV diagnostic）\n151\t    是必要的，因为不同 connector 需要不同的 compression strategy。MLP projector 应用 simple  pruning（已有\n152\t    graded degradation），pixel-shuffle 应用 VTR re-encoding。\n153\t\n154\t    '\n155\t- name: OpenVLA VTC M-sweep training (M=32/64/96)\n156\t  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n157\t  description: 'OpenVLA VTC-only（无 backbone fine-tuning）M-sweep 训练。此前 M=96_v3 和 M=64_v3  均报\n158\t    failed/negative。预测所有 M 值均无法恢复 SR，与 c4_ext 一致。\n159\t\n160\t    '\n161\t  expected_results:\n162\t    m32_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n163\t    m64_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n164\t    m96_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n165\t    training_loss_converges: true\n166\t    eval_sr_zero: true\n167\t    diagnosis: VTC learns to minimize training loss but does not transfer to closed-loop\n168\t      control\n169\t  result_rationale: 'VTC-only 模式冻结了 backbone，仅训练 22M compressor 参数。对 MLP projector，\n170\t    backbone 已经学习了 per-token semantically meaningful representations。VTC  强制将 256\n171\t    个有独立语义的 token 映射到更少的 query token，丢失了 token-level  semantic granularity。训练 loss\n172\t    收敛（因为 cross-attention 可以学习压缩映射） 但 closed-loop control 失败，因为 action prediction\n173\t    依赖 fine-grained token  discrimination 而非 compressed summary。与 SmolVLA 不同，SmolVLA\n174\t    的 pixel-shuffle  token 本身缺乏 individual semantics（每个 token 编码 32×32 pixel region），\n175\t    VTR re-encoding 只需恢复 spatial structure 而非 semantic content。\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t  tables: []\n179\t  figures_description: []\n180\t  analysis: '所有 M 值失败构成 c4_ext 的完整 ablation：VTR 的有效性严格绑定到 pixel-shuffle  connector\n181\t    的空间纠缠修复功能。Paper 中作为 §5.3 \"Re-encoding mechanism\" 的 反面证据，说明 VTR 不是通用 token compressor。\n182\t\n183\t    '\n184\t- name: X-VLA cliff threshold 3-seed localization\n185\t  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n186\t  description: 'X-VLA k=0.8 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位已完成。 k=0.80=89.0±0.72pp, k=0.85=67.9±0.31pp。Non-monotonic\n187\t    recovery 确认。\n188\t\n189\t    '\n190\t  expected_results:\n191\t    k080_3seed_mean: 89.0\n192\t    k080_3seed_std: 0.72\n193\t    k085_3seed_mean: 67.9\n194\t    k085_3seed_std: 0.31\n195\t    nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n196\t    cliff_zone: k=0.82-0.87\n197\t    deterministic_sd_below_1pp: true\n198\t  result_rationale: 'BART encoder（12 层 transformer）在 42 tokens（k=0.85）时触发 length-dependent  interaction\n199\t    breakdown。42 tokens 是 BART 自注意力模式的临界密度——低于此密度， BART 的 cross-token mixing 产生的依赖链被截断，导致\n200\t    cascading information loss。 40 tokens（k=0.8）反而恢复，因为 token 密度进一步降低使 BART 退化为  near-independent\n201\t    processing（类似纯 linear projection 行为）。SD<1pp 证明这是  完全 deterministic 的架构属性，非随机效应。3-seed\n202\t    一致性消除了训练 seed 混淆因素。\n203\t\n204\t    '\n205\t  tables:\n206\t  - title: 'Table: X-VLA cliff localization (L2norm, 3-seed)'\n207\t    columns:\n208\t    - k\n209\t    - Tokens kept\n210\t    - Seed 42\n211\t    - Seed 43\n212\t    - Seed 44\n213\t    - Mean±SD\n214\t    data:\n215\t    - - '0.90'\n216\t      - '45'\n217\t      - '97.6'\n218\t      - '98.2'\n219\t      - '99.4'\n220\t      - 98.4±0.9\n221\t    - - '0.85'\n222\t      - '42'\n223\t      - '68.0'\n224\t      - '67.6'\n225\t      - '68.2'\n226\t      - 67.9±0.3\n227\t    - - '0.80'\n228\t      - '40'\n229\t      - '88.8'\n230\t      - '88.4'\n231\t      - '89.8'\n232\t      - 89.0±0.7\n233\t    - - '0.70'\n234\t      - '35'\n235\t      - '56.2'\n236\t      - '58.2'\n237\t      - '56.4'\n238\t      - 56.9±1.1\n239\t  figures_description:\n240\t  - 'Fig: X-VLA pruning curve with cliff zone highlighted. k=0.85 dip (67.9%) below\n241\t    k=0.8 (89.0%) creating non-monotonic pattern. Error bars from 3-seed.'\n242\t  analysis: 'Cliff 定位精确到 k=0.82-0.87 区间。Non-monotonicity 是 BART encoder 的 emergent  property：存在一个\n243\t    critical token density 使得 BART self-attention 的 cross-token  mixing 恰好最大化 information\n244\t    cascading damage。Paper figure 将此作为  token-entangling connector 的典型特征展示。\n245\t\n246\t    '\n247\t- name: OFT token importance CV measurement\n248\t  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n249\t  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT CV 已从 openvla_entropy_real 和 analysis 中确认为 0.219。 Entropy=0.667≈Standard(0.661)。完成\n250\t    5/5 model diagnostic table。\n251\t\n252\t    '\n253\t  expected_results:\n254\t    oft_cv: 0.219\n255\t    oft_entropy: 0.667\n256\t    standard_openvla_cv: 0.215\n257\t    cv_delta_oft_vs_standard: 0.004\n258\t    entropy_delta: 0.006\n259\t    connector_determines_attention: true\n260\t  result_rationale: 'OFT 与 Standard OpenVLA 共享相同的 3-layer MLP connector（DINOv2+SigLIP\n261\t    fusion  仅增加输入通道但不改变 MLP mixing 结构）。Action head 差异（OFT diffusion vs  Standard autoregressive）不影响\n262\t    vision token attention 分布，因为 attention  pattern 由 connector 在 vision-LLM 接口处决定，action\n263\t    head 在 LLM output 端操作。 CV 0.219≈0.215 差异在 noise level（<0.01），证明 connector 是 attention\n264\t    structure  的唯一决定因素。\n265\t\n266\t    '\n267\t  tables:\n268\t  - title: 'Table: Complete 6-model diagnostic spectrum'\n269\t    columns:\n270\t    - Model\n271\t    - Connector\n272\t    - Params\n273\t    - Tokens\n274\t    - Entropy\n275\t    - CV\n276\t    - Pruning Class\n277\t    data:\n278\t    - - pi0\n279\t      - Pure linear\n280\t      - 3.3B\n281\t      - '256'\n282\t      - '0.959'\n283\t      - '0.038'\n284\t      - Immune\n285\t    - - pi0.5\n286\t      - Pure linear (x sqrt_d)\n287\t      - 4B\n288\t      - '768'\n289\t      - ~0.67\n290\t      - '0.055'\n291\t      - Uniformly Critical\n292\t    - - X-VLA\n293\t      - Linear+BART 12L\n294\t      - 880M\n295\t      - '50'\n296\t      - '0.614'\n297\t      - '0.151'\n298\t      - Threshold-graded\n299\t    - - OpenVLA\n300\t      - 3-layer MLP\n301\t      - 7B\n302\t      - '256'\n303\t      - '0.661'\n304\t      - '0.215'\n305\t      - Smooth graded\n306\t    - - OFT\n307\t      - 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\n308\t      - 7B\n309\t      - '512'\n310\t      - '0.667'\n311\t      - '0.219'\n312\t      - Smooth graded (expected)\n313\t    - - SmolVLA\n314\t      - Pixel-shuffle 16x\n315\t      - 450M\n316\t      - '128'\n317\t      - '0.952'\n318\t      - '0.314'\n319\t      - Catastrophic\n320\t  figures_description: []\n321\t  analysis: '6-model diagnostic table 完整化。CV 连续谱 0.038→0.314 无间断地预测 pruning tolerance。\n322\t    OFT entry 作为 action head 对照实验消除了\"action head 影响 pruning\"的替代假说。\n323\t\n324\t    '\n325\t- name: Cross-suite 2-axis framework validation (5 models × 4 suites)\n326\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n327\t  description: '5 models × 4 LIBERO suites × 2 methods（L2norm/random）全矩阵填充。 已收集绝大部分数据。剩余：OpenVLA\n328\t    Spatial random k=0.9, OpenVLA Long L2norm/random k=0.9, 部分 OpenVLA attention cross-suite。预测所有剩余数据点与\n329\t    2-axis framework 一致。\n330\t\n331\t    '\n332\t  expected_results:\n333\t    xvla_object_k09_sr: 97.6\n334\t    xvla_goal_k09_sr: 70.2\n335\t    xvla_long_k09_sr: 27.5\n336\t    xvla_amplification_object_to_goal_pp: 27.4\n337\t    xvla_amplification_object_to_long_pp: 70.1\n338\t    pi05_l2norm_object_k09_sr: 98.2\n339\t    pi05_l2norm_goal_k09_sr: 90.6\n340\t    pi05_l2norm_long_k09_sr: 81.0\n341\t    pi05_amplification_object_to_goal_pp: 7.6\n342\t    pi05_amplification_object_to_long_pp: 17.2\n343\t    openvla_spatial_random_k09_sr: 67.0\n344\t    openvla_long_l2norm_k09_sr: 46.0\n345\t    openvla_long_random_k09_sr: 43.0\n346\t    smolvla_spatial_k095_sr: 0.0\n347\t    smolvla_goal_k095_sr: 0.0\n348\t    smolvla_long_k095_sr: 0.0\n349\t    cross_suite_framework_accuracy_pct: 95\n350\t    axis2_amplification_entangling_min_pp: 27.4\n351\t    axis2_amplification_independent_max_pp: 17.2\n352\t  result_rationale: \"Axis-2（task complexity）放大效应的机制：complex tasks（Goal/Long）要求 multi-step\\\n353\t    \\  reasoning，每一步的 action prediction 依赖前一步保留的 spatial information。 Token-entangling\\\n354\t    \\ connectors（BART/pixel-shuffle）的 pruning damage 在 multi-step  中 compound——单步小损失在序列中累积为大损失。Token-independent\\\n355\t    \\ connectors（linear/MLP） 的 pruning damage 是 per-step 局部的，不会 cascade。\\n具体预测依据：\\\n356\t    \\ - X-VLA Object→Goal 27.4pp 已确认（same k=0.9, same method, only task differs） -\\\n357\t    \\ X-VLA Object→Long 更大（70.1pp）因为 Long 任务平均 horizon 更长，compounding 更严重 - π0.5 L2norm\\\n358\t    \\ Object→Goal 仅 7.6pp（low CV 使得 L2norm 选择的 token 在 spatial \\n  coverage 上已近最优，task\\\n359\t    \\ complexity 无法放大 spatial coverage 的已有优势）\\n- π0.5 Object→Long 17.2pp 稍大，但仍 <20pp（independent\\\n360\t    \\ connector 上限）\\nOpenVLA 剩余预测： - Spatial random k=0.9≈67%：OpenVLA Spatial baseline=80%,\\\n361\t    \\ L2norm k=0.9=75%。\\n  Random 通常比 L2norm 低 5-8pp（CV=0.215 使 L2norm 有轻微优势）\\n- Long\\\n362\t    \\ L2norm k=0.9≈46%：Long baseline=52.8%, 相对保留率≈OpenVLA Object pattern - Long random\\\n363\t    \\ k=0.9≈43%：随机稍差于 L2norm（high CV）\\nSmolVLA 全 suite 0%：pixel-shuffle 纠缠在任何 task\\\n364\t    \\ distribution 下都导致 catastrophic  failure。Spatial/Goal 的 baseline 较低（44.6%/60.8%）不影响\\\n365\t    \\ cliff-edge——即使 baseline  更低，k=0.95 pruning 仍然 collapse 至 0%。\\n\"\n366\t  tables:\n367\t  - title: 'Table: 2-Axis Framework — Axis-2 amplification at k=0.9 (L2norm)'\n368\t    columns:\n369\t    - Model\n370\t    - CV\n371\t    - Connector\n372\t    - Object SR(%)\n373\t    - Spatial SR(%)\n374\t    - Goal SR(%)\n375\t    - Long SR(%)\n376\t    - Amplif O→G (pp)\n377\t    data:\n378\t    - - pi0.5\n379\t      - '0.055'\n380\t      - Linear\n381\t      - '98.2'\n382\t      - '95.0'\n383\t      - '90.6'\n384\t      - '81.0'\n385\t      - '7.6'\n386\t    - - X-VLA\n387\t      - '0.151'\n388\t      - Lin+BART\n389\t      - '97.6'\n390\t      - '78.8'\n391\t      - '70.2'\n392\t      - '27.5'\n393\t      - '27.4'\n394\t    - - OpenVLA\n395\t      - '0.215'\n396\t      - MLP\n397\t      - '70.6'\n398\t      - '75.0'\n399\t      - '74.8'\n400\t      - '46.0'\n401\t      - -4.2*\n402\t    - - SmolVLA\n403\t      - '0.314'\n404\t      - Pix-shuf\n405\t      - '0.0'\n406\t      - '0.0'\n407\t      - '0.0'\n408\t      - '0.0'\n409\t      - N/A\n410\t  - title: 'Table: Cross-suite pruning sensitivity heatmap (SR at k=0.5, random)'\n411\t    columns:\n412\t    - Model\n413\t    - Object\n414\t    - Spatial\n415\t    - Goal\n416\t    - Long\n417\t    data:\n418\t    - - pi0.5\n419\t      - 69.4 (68.9†)\n420\t      - '71.6'\n421\t      - '73.6'\n422\t      - '46.8'\n423\t    - - X-VLA\n424\t      - 70.6 (70.3†)\n425\t      - '71.4'\n426\t      - 67.9†\n427\t      - '61.6'\n428\t    - - OpenVLA\n429\t      - '35.8'\n430\t      - ~36\n431\t      - '52.2'\n432\t      - ~35\n433\t    - - SmolVLA\n434\t      - '0.0'\n435\t      - '0.6'\n436\t      - '0.0'\n437\t      - '0.0'\n438\t  figures_description:\n439\t  - 'Fig: 2-axis heatmap — rows=models (sorted by CV), columns=suites (sorted by complexity).\n440\t    Color=SR at k=0.9. Clear gradient: entangling connectors show steep color change\n441\t    across suites, independent connectors show mild change.'\n442\t  - 'Fig: Amplification bar chart — grouped bars per model showing Object→Goal SR\n443\t    drop (pp). X-VLA 27.4pp tower vs π0.5 7.6pp bar. Horizontal line at 20pp separating\n444\t    entangling/independent zones.'\n445\t  analysis: '2-axis framework 在 95% 的 model×suite cells 中正确预测 pruning outcome。 唯一的\n446\t    partial exception：OpenVLA Goal k=0.9 SR（74.8%）高于 Object k=0.9（70.6%）， 但这是 baseline\n447\t    difference（Goal baseline 74.8% = Object baseline 74%），相对  degradation 是一致的。Framework\n448\t    accuracy 95% 落在 best tier 范围 [90, 100] 内。\n449\t\n450\t    Key axis-2 interaction：entangling connectors 放大倍数 27.4pp（X-VLA Object→Goal） 落在\n451\t    best tier 范围 [25, 45] 内。Independent connectors 保持 ≤10pp（π0.5 7.6pp） 符合假设。Long\n452\t    suite 的更大放大（X-VLA 70.1pp, π0.5 17.2pp）与 horizon length  正相关，进一步验证 compounding\n453\t    damage 机制。\n454\t\n455\t    '\n456\t- name: VTR cross-suite generalization (SmolVLA Long)\n457\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n458\t  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M=32 已在 Spatial（53.2%）和 Goal（56.4%）验证。 剩余：Long suite（baseline\n459\t    36.6%）的 VTR recovery。 预测 M=32 Long≈33-38%，完成 Diagnose-then-Compress 全 suite 验证。\n460\t\n461\t    '\n462\t  expected_results:\n463\t    smolvla_long_baseline_sr: 36.6\n464\t    smolvla_long_hard_prune_k05_sr: 0.0\n465\t    smolvla_long_hard_prune_k095_sr: 0.0\n466\t    vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.5\n467\t    vtr_m32_long_ci95_lower: 31.0\n468\t    vtr_m32_long_ci95_upper: 40.0\n469\t    vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2\n470\t    vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4\n471\t    vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1\n472\t    recovery_ratio_long: 0.97\n473\t    cross_suite_recovery_consistent: true\n474\t  result_rationale: \"VTR cross-suite recovery ratio 预测≈0.97（35.5/36.6）：\\n1. M-curve\\\n475\t    \\ 平坦性在 Object suite 已确认——VTR 的 re-encoding 修复 spatial \\n   entanglement，这是 connector-level\\\n476\t    \\ 属性，与 task distribution 无关。\\n2. Spatial recovery 53.2%/43.8%=1.21 和 Goal recovery\\\n477\t    \\ 56.4%/60.8%=0.93 \\n   显示 cross-suite recovery ratio 围绕 1.0 波动（±20%），中位数 ≈1.0。\\n\\\n478\t    3. Long suite baseline 较低（36.6% vs Object 59.2%）因为 Long 任务本身更难，\\n   但 VTR 不应额外降低——它只修复\\\n479\t    \\ pruning damage，不影响 task difficulty。\\n4. Long 的稍低 recovery（预测 0.97）可能源于 Long\\\n480\t    \\ horizon 放大了 VTR \\n   re-encoding 中的微小信息损失，但效果应 <5pp。\\n\\nVTR 在 Long 上仍将远超 hard\\\n481\t    \\ pruning（35.5% vs 0%），完成全 4 suites 的  \\\"recovery from cliff-edge\\\" 证据链。\\n\"\n482\t  tables:\n483\t  - title: 'Table: VTR M=32 cross-suite recovery'\n484\t    columns:\n485\t    - Suite\n486\t    - Baseline SR(%)\n487\t    - Hard prune k=0.5 SR(%)\n488\t    - VTR M=32 SR(%)\n489\t    - Recovery ratio\n490\t    data:\n491\t    - - Object\n492\t      - '59.2'\n493\t      - '0.0'\n494\t      - '60.1'\n495\t      - '1.015'\n496\t    - - Spatial\n497\t      - 43.8*\n498\t      - '0.6'\n499\t      - '53.2'\n500\t      - 1.21*\n501\t    - - Goal\n502\t      - 60.8*\n503\t      - '0.0'\n504\t      - '56.4'\n505\t      - '0.93'\n506\t    - - Long\n507\t      - '36.6'\n508\t      - '0.0'\n509\t      - 35.5 (pred)\n510\t      - 0.97 (pred)\n511\t  figures_description:\n512\t  - 'Fig: VTR recovery bar chart — 4 suites side by side, each showing baseline (gray),\n513\t    hard prune (red, near 0), VTR M=32 (green, near baseline). Consistent recovery\n514\t    pattern across all suites.'\n515\t  analysis: 'VTR cross-suite generalization证明 re-encoding 修复的是 architectural entanglement  而非\n516\t    task-specific information。Recovery ratio ≈1.0 across 4 suites 支持 Claim 4： \"Learned\n517\t    Re-Encoding Achieves Near-Lossless Compression Where Deletion Fails\"。 vtr_smolvla_recovery_ratio\n518\t    0.97 落在 best tier 范围 [0.95, 1.05] 内。\n519\t\n520\t    对 practitioner 的 implication：使用 pixel-shuffle connector 的 VLA 可以通过  VTR 实现任意压缩比而无显著\n521\t    SR 损失。22M 额外参数 + 6% latency overhead 是可接受的代价。\n522\t\n523\t    '\n524\t- name: π0.5 uniformly critical behavior cross-suite validation\n525\t  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n526\t  description: 'π0.5（4B, PaliGemma linear proj）已完成 4 suites baseline + 全面 pruning\n527\t    sweep。 CV=0.055 confirmed。L2norm plateau（k≥0.85 maintains ≥98% Object, ≥88% Spatial/Goal）\n528\t    和 random cliff（k=0.85-0.925 Object collapse）均已 multi-seed 验证。 Scaling law extreme（Δ(R-L2)=+36pp\n529\t    at k=0.5）confirmed。 剩余工作：Cross-suite 一致性最终确认 + paper narrative 整合。\n530\t\n531\t    '\n532\t  expected_results:\n533\t    baseline_object: 98.2\n534\t    baseline_spatial: 97.2\n535\t    baseline_goal: 96.4\n536\t    baseline_long: 92.8\n537\t    cv: 0.055\n538\t    l2norm_k095_object: 98.2\n539\t    l2norm_k09_object: 98.2\n540\t    l2norm_k085_object: 98.0\n541\t    l2norm_k095_spatial: 97.8\n542\t    l2norm_k09_spatial: 95.0\n543\t    l2norm_k085_spatial: 88.6\n544\t    l2norm_k095_goal: 90.8\n545\t    l2norm_k09_goal: 90.6\n546\t    l2norm_k085_goal: 88.0\n547\t    l2norm_k095_long: 87.0\n548\t    l2norm_k09_long: 81.0\n549\t    l2norm_k085_long: 78.4\n550\t    random_k095_object: 74.0\n551\t    random_k0925_object: 27.6\n552\t    random_k09_object: 9.0\n553\t    random_k085_object: 5.0\n554\t    random_k095_spatial: 76.4\n555\t    random_k0925_spatial: 58.2\n556\t    random_k09_spatial: 54.6\n557\t    random_k085_spatial: 60.2\n558\t    random_k095_goal: 83.8\n559\t    random_k0925_goal: 70.0\n560\t    random_k09_goal: 62.2\n561\t    random_k085_goal: 52.4\n562\t    random_k095_long: 63.2\n563\t    random_k09_long: 31.8\n564\t    random_k085_long: 45.2\n565\t    l2norm_k05_object: 33.4\n566\t    random_k05_object: 69.4\n567\t    gap_R_minus_L2_k05_pp: 36.0\n568\t    l2norm_k05_spatial: 55.6\n569\t    random_k05_spatial: 71.6\n570\t    gap_spatial_k05_pp: 16.0\n571\t    l2norm_k05_goal: 59.8\n572\t    random_k05_goal: 73.6\n573\t    gap_goal_k05_pp: 13.8\n574\t    l2norm_k05_long: 50.2\n575\t    random_k05_long: 46.8\n576\t    gap_long_k05_pp: -3.4\n577\t  result_rationale: \"π0.5 \\\"uniformly critical\\\" 行为的 cross-suite 一致性验证了 Claim 1 和\\\n578\t    \\ Claim 5：\\n1. **L2norm plateau 跨 suite 一致**：k≥0.85 时 L2norm 在所有 4 suites 维持高\\\n579\t    \\ SR\\n   （Object 98%, Spatial 88.6%, Goal 88%, Long 78.4%）。Plateau 随 task complexity\\\n580\t    \\ \\n   轻微下降但保持>78%。机制：L2norm 的 deterministic selection 保留 spatial coverage，\\n\\\n581\t    \\   low CV（0.055）使选中的 token subset 具有 near-uniform importance，覆盖度好。\\n\\n2. **Random\\\n582\t    \\ cliff 跨 suite 差异化**：\\n   - Object cliff dramatic（74→28→9→5%），因为 Object tasks\\\n583\t    \\ 有 concentrated critical \\n     tokens（object identity discrimination 依赖 specific\\\n584\t    \\ patches）\\n   - Spatial cliff milder（76→58→55→60%），因为 spatial layout information\\\n585\t    \\ 是 \\n     distributed 的，random removal 不会完全摧毁 spatial signal\\n   - Goal cliff\\\n586\t    \\ moderate（84→70→62→52%），因为 Goal tasks 混合了 spatial 和 \\n     semantic disambiguation\\n\\\n587\t    \\   - Long cliff steep（63→32→45%），因为 long-horizon compounding 放大了 random \\n  \\\n588\t    \\   token loss\\n\\n3. **Scaling law（Δ(R-L2)）cross-suite 演变**：\\n   - Object k=0.5:\\\n589\t    \\ +36.0pp（random wins massively, extreme of scaling law）\\n   - Spatial k=0.5:\\\n590\t    \\ +16.0pp（random wins, spatial distributed info helps random）\\n   - Goal k=0.5:\\\n591\t    \\ +13.8pp（random wins, similar to spatial）\\n   - Long k=0.5: -3.4pp（L2norm slightly\\\n592\t    \\ wins — long horizon 使 L2norm 的 \\n     deterministic consistency 成为优势，random\\\n593\t    \\ 的 per-step variance compounds）\\n   \\n   Gap 从 +36→+16→+14→-3.4 的变化不违反 scaling\\\n594\t    \\ law：scaling law 是 \\n   cross-model（CV drives direction），不是 cross-suite。Suite\\\n595\t    \\ 影响 gap \\n   magnitude 但不改变 sign（除 Long 的轻微 reversal，可解释为 horizon effect）。\\n\"\n596\t  tables:\n597\t  - title: 'Table: π0.5 L2norm plateau cross-suite'\n598\t    columns:\n599\t    - k\n600\t    - Object\n601\t    - Spatial\n602\t    - Goal\n603\t    - Long\n604\t    data:\n605\t    - - 1.0 (baseline)\n606\t      - '98.2'\n607\t      - '97.2'\n608\t      - '96.4'\n609\t      - '92.8'\n610\t    - - '0.95'\n611\t      - '98.2'\n612\t      - '97.8'\n613\t      - '90.8'\n614\t      - '87.0'\n615\t    - - '0.925'\n616\t      - '99.2'\n617\t      - '97.0'\n618\t      - '89.8'\n619\t      - —\n620\t    - - '0.9'\n621\t      - '98.2'\n622\t      - '95.0'\n623\t      - '90.6'\n624\t      - '81.0'\n625\t    - - '0.85'\n626\t      - '98.0'\n627\t      - '88.6'\n628\t      - '88.0'\n629\t      - '78.4'\n630\t    - - '0.7'\n631\t      - '55.0'\n632\t      - '67.0'\n633\t      - '73.6'\n634\t      - '62.6'\n635\t    - - '0.5'\n636\t      - '33.4'\n637\t      - '55.6'\n638\t      - '59.8'\n639\t      - '50.2'\n640\t    - - '0.3'\n641\t      - '51.0'\n642\t      - '57.2'\n643\t      - '50.6'\n644\t      - '36.6'\n645\t  - title: 'Table: π0.5 random cliff cross-suite'\n646\t    columns:\n647\t    - k\n648\t    - Object\n649\t    - Spatial\n650\t    - Goal\n651\t    - Long\n652\t    data:\n653\t    - - '0.95'\n654\t      - '74.0'\n655\t      - '76.4'\n656\t      - '83.8'\n657\t      - '63.2'\n658\t    - - '0.925'\n659\t      - '27.6'\n660\t      - '58.2'\n661\t      - '70.0'\n662\t      - —\n663\t    - - '0.9'\n664\t      - '9.0'\n665\t      - '54.6'\n666\t      - '62.2'\n667\t      - '31.8'\n668\t    - - '0.85'\n669\t      - '5.0'\n670\t      - '60.2'\n671\t      - '52.4'\n672\t      - '45.2'\n673\t    - - '0.7'\n674\t      - '75.5'\n675\t      - '74.4'\n676\t      - '75.6'\n677\t      - '65.8'\n678\t    - - '0.5'\n679\t      - '69.4'\n680\t      - '71.6'\n681\t      - '73.6'\n682\t      - '46.8'\n683\t    - - '0.3'\n684\t      - '36.4'\n685\t      - '43.4'\n686\t      - '52.8'\n687\t      - '29.6'\n688\t  figures_description:\n689\t  - 'Fig: π0.5 L2norm vs random pruning curves, 4 suites side-by-side. L2norm plateau\n690\t    vs random cliff contrast. Object cliff most dramatic, Spatial most resilient.'\n691\t  - 'Fig: Concentrated vs distributed critical tokens illustration — Object tasks\n692\t    show localized critical patches, Spatial tasks show diffuse importance.'\n693\t  analysis: 'π0.5 完整 cross-suite 数据确认了核心假设 3：uniformly critical behavior  generalize\n694\t    至 Spatial/Goal，且机制一致（concentrated vs distributed critical tokens  决定 cliff severity）。pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp=36.0pp\n695\t    落在 best tier  范围 [30, 40] 内。\n696\t\n697\t    π0.5 是 scaling law 的 extreme point（CV=0.055, 最低），在所有 suite 上都展现 L2norm catastrophic\n698\t    failure at aggressive compression。这强化了 \"CV predicts optimal  pruning strategy\"\n699\t    narrative——对 low-CV models，importance-based pruning actively harmful。\n700\t\n701\t    '\n702\t- name: OpenVLA-OFT graded degradation cross-suite validation\n703\t  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n704\t  description: 'OFT（7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fusion, 512 tokens）在兼容硬件（A100+torch2.2）\n705\t    上进行 4 suites baseline + pruning 评估。CV=0.219≈OpenVLA(0.215) 预测相同的  graded degradation\n706\t    模式。此实验验证 action head（OFT vs Standard）不影响 pruning behavior。\n707\t\n708\t    '\n709\t  expected_results:\n710\t    baseline_object: 97.0\n711\t    baseline_spatial: 95.0\n712\t    baseline_goal: 96.0\n713\t    baseline_long: 85.0\n714\t    l2norm_k095_object: 91.0\n715\t    l2norm_k09_object: 83.0\n716\t    l2norm_k07_object: 65.0\n717\t    l2norm_k05_object: 50.0\n718\t    l2norm_k03_object: 28.0\n719\t    random_k095_object: 90.0\n720\t    random_k09_object: 80.0\n721\t    random_k07_object: 60.0\n722\t    random_k05_object: 46.0\n723\t    random_k03_object: 25.0\n724\t    gap_R_minus_L2_k05_object_pp: -4.0\n725\t    gap_R_minus_L2_k07_object_pp: -5.0\n726\t    l2norm_k09_spatial: 82.0\n727\t    l2norm_k09_goal: 84.0\n728\t    l2norm_k09_long: 68.0\n729\t    cv: 0.219\n730\t    entropy: 0.667\n731\t  result_rationale: \"OFT 使用与 Standard OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector。CV 0.219≈0.215\\\n732\t    \\ 的高度一致性 预测几乎相同的 pruning degradation pattern：\\n1. **Graded degradation 预测**：OpenVLA\\\n733\t    \\ relative retention at k=0.5 = 37.4/74 = 50.5%。\\n   OFT baseline 更高（~97%），absolute\\\n734\t    \\ SR 更高但 relative pattern 一致。\\n   预测 OFT k=0.5 L2norm ≈ 97×0.515 ≈ 50%。\\n\\n2.\\\n735\t    \\ **L2norm > random 一致**：high CV（0.219）= meaningful importance differentiation\\\n736\t    \\ → \\n   L2norm selection effective。预测 L2norm 在所有 k 值优于 random 3-6pp，\\n   与 OpenVLA\\\n737\t    \\ pattern（+1.4 to +5.4pp）一致。\\n\\n3. **Cross-suite pattern**：OFT 的 512 tokens（vs\\\n738\t    \\ OpenVLA 256）提供更高的信息冗余，\\n   可能使 pruning tolerance 略高于 OpenVLA。但 connector mechanism\\\n739\t    \\ 相同，\\n   degradation shape 应一致（smooth graded）。\\n\\n4. **Action head 独立性**：OFT\\\n740\t    \\ diffusion action head 和 Standard autoregressive \\n   action head 对 pruning 的反应应\\\n741\t    \\ identical，因为 pruning 发生在 vision-LLM \\n   接口而非 action decode 阶段。这是 connector-determines-pruning\\\n742\t    \\ 假说的关键证据。\\n\"\n743\t  tables:\n744\t  - title: 'Table: OFT vs OpenVLA pruning comparison (Object suite, L2norm)'\n745\t    columns:\n746\t    - k\n747\t    - OFT SR(%) (pred)\n748\t    - OpenVLA SR(%)\n749\t    - OFT retention\n750\t    - OpenVLA retention\n751\t    data:\n752\t    - - '1.0'\n753\t      - '97.0'\n754\t      - '74.0'\n755\t      - 100%\n756\t      - 100%\n757\t    - - '0.95'\n758\t      - '91.0'\n759\t      - '69.4'\n760\t      - 93.8%\n761\t      - 93.8%\n762\t    - - '0.9'\n763\t      - '83.0'\n764\t      - '62.0'\n765\t      - 85.6%\n766\t      - 83.8%\n767\t    - - '0.7'\n768\t      - '65.0'\n769\t      - '49.0'\n770\t      - 67.0%\n771\t      - 66.2%\n772\t    - - '0.5'\n773\t      - '50.0'\n774\t      - '37.4'\n775\t      - 51.5%\n776\t      - 50.5%\n777\t    - - '0.3'\n778\t      - '28.0'\n779\t      - '20.6'\n780\t      - 28.9%\n781\t      - 27.8%\n782\t  figures_description:\n783\t  - 'Fig: OFT vs OpenVLA pruning curves overlaid, normalized by baseline. Near-identical\n784\t    relative degradation pattern despite different baselines and action heads.'\n785\t  analysis: 'OFT 实验是 paper 中消除 confound 的关键 ablation：same connector + different action\n786\t    head  → same pruning behavior，证明 connector 是 causal factor。如果 Blackwell GPU  兼容性问题无法解决，OFT\n787\t    可以仅通过 CV/entropy analysis（已完成）纳入 paper， 辅以 official baseline 引用。LIBERO eval 是\n788\t    bonus（icing on the cake）， CV/entropy 已足够支持 Claim。\n789\t\n790\t    '\n791\t- name: Perceiver Resampler connector fine-tune + pruning\n792\t  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n793\t  description: 'RoboFlamingo（Perceiver Resampler: 64 learned query tokens 通过 cross-attention  attend\n794\t    to vision patches）在 LIBERO Object 上 fine-tune 后进行 pruning sweep。 验证第 4 种 connector\n795\t    family 的 pruning behavior。此前训练尝试因基础设施问题被 kill。\n796\t\n797\t    '\n798\t  expected_results:\n799\t    baseline_object_sr: 58.0\n800\t    baseline_ci95:\n801\t    - 53.5\n802\t    - 62.4\n803\t    l2norm_k095_sr: 52.0\n804\t    l2norm_k09_sr: 42.0\n805\t    l2norm_k07_sr: 22.0\n806\t    l2norm_k05_sr: 10.0\n807\t    random_k095_sr: 50.0\n808\t    random_k09_sr: 38.0\n809\t    random_k07_sr: 18.0\n810\t    random_k05_sr: 8.0\n811\t    importance_cv: 0.22\n812\t    entropy_ratio: 0.82\n813\t    connector_class: token-entangling (cross-attention)\n814\t    pruning_pattern: steep graded → threshold at k≈0.7\n815\t  result_rationale: \"Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 机制创造了中等程度的 token entanglement：\\n\\\n816\t    1. **Entanglement 机制**：64 query tokens 各自通过 cross-attention attend 全部 vision \\n\\\n817\t    \\   patches。每个 output token 不再对应特定 spatial region（unlike linear proj），\\n   而是\\\n818\t    \\ learned mixture of all patches。但与 pixel-shuffle 不同，这种 mixture \\n   是 learned\\\n819\t    \\ 的且 query-specific，因此不同 query 可能 specialize to different \\n   spatial/semantic\\\n820\t    \\ aspects。\\n\\n2. **CV 预测 ~0.22**：介于 X-VLA（0.151）和 SmolVLA（0.314）之间。\\n   Cross-attention\\\n821\t    \\ 创造的依赖比 BART sequential mixing 更直接但不如 pixel-shuffle \\n   的空间折叠极端。Query specialization\\\n822\t    \\ 产生 moderate importance heterogeneity。\\n\\n3. **Pruning pattern 预测**：steep graded\\\n823\t    \\ degradation。k=0.95 开始可见 drop \\n   （~10% relative），k=0.7 显著下降（~60% relative），k=0.5\\\n824\t    \\ 接近 collapse。\\n   比 OpenVLA/MLP 更陡但不如 SmolVLA/pixel-shuffle catastrophic。\\n\\n\\\n825\t    4. **Baseline 预测 ~58%**：first-attempt fine-tuning on LIBERO，\\n   RoboFlamingo\\\n826\t    \\ original architecture 不是为 LIBERO 任务优化的。\\n   合理的 mid-range SR。\\n\\n5. **L2norm\\\n827\t    \\ ≈ random**：CV ~0.22 处于 L2norm 和 random 的交叉区域，\\n   两种方法差异应 <5pp，类似 OpenVLA pattern。\\n\"\n828\t  tables:\n829\t  - title: 'Table: Perceiver Resampler pruning curve (predicted)'\n830\t    columns:\n831\t    - k\n832\t    - Tokens kept\n833\t    - L2norm SR(%)\n834\t    - Random SR(%)\n835\t    - Δ(R-L2)\n836\t    data:\n837\t    - - '1.0'\n838\t      - '64'\n839\t      - '58.0'\n840\t      - '58.0'\n841\t      - '0'\n842\t    - - '0.95'\n843\t      - '61'\n844\t      - '52.0'\n845\t      - '50.0'\n846\t      - '-2.0'\n847\t    - - '0.9'\n848\t      - '58'\n849\t      - '42.0'\n850\t      - '38.0'\n851\t      - '-4.0'\n852\t    - - '0.7'\n853\t      - '45'\n854\t      - '22.0'\n855\t      - '18.0'\n856\t      - '-4.0'\n857\t    - - '0.5'\n858\t      - '32'\n859\t      - '10.0'\n860\t      - '8.0'\n861\t      - '-2.0'\n862\t  figures_description:\n863\t  - 'Fig: 4-connector family pruning curves on same axes — Linear (π0.5, flat), MLP\n864\t    (OpenVLA, gradual), Perceiver (RoboFlamingo, steep graded), Pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA,\n865\t    cliff). Continuous spectrum of pruning tolerance.'\n866\t  analysis: 'Perceiver Resampler 填补了 connector spectrum 的空白——在 MLP（graded）和 pixel-shuffle  （catastrophic）之间提供了第\n867\t    4 个 data point。如果 CV ~0.22 且 pruning pattern  呈 steep graded，它将进一步验证 CV 作为 continuous\n868\t    predictor 的有效性。\n869\t\n870\t    对 paper 的贡献：从 3 connector families 扩展到 4，增加了 paper 的 generalizability。 但即使此实验因基础设施问题未完成，paper\n871\t    已有 5 models × 3 families 的充分覆盖， Perceiver 可作为 future work 提及。在 best tier 下，此实验成功完成并增加\n872\t    paper  的 reviewer 说服力。\n873\t\n874\t    '\n875\t- name: E5 attention-based pruning — correct importance metric for entangling connectors\n876\t  plan_id: e5_attention_pruning_xvla\n877\t  description: 'X-VLA attention-based token pruning（last-layer / mean / rollout）在\n878\t    4 suites 上验证。 核心发现：attention-based importance 在 entangling connector 上远优于 L2norm，\n879\t    因为 attention 捕获了 BART encoder 创造的 cross-token dependencies。 已有数据覆盖 Object/Spatial/Goal/Long\n880\t    at k=0.5 和 k=0.3/k=0.7 部分点。 Goal suite 泛化已确认（SR=96.8-98.2% at k=0.5）。\n881\t\n882\t    '\n883\t  expected_results:\n884\t    attn_last_obj_k05: 99.2\n885\t    attn_mean_obj_k05: 98.4\n886\t    attn_rollout_obj_k05: 97.4\n887\t    attn_last_obj_k07: 99.2\n888\t    attn_last_obj_k03: 84.2\n889\t    attn_mean_obj_k03: 96.0\n890\t    attn_rollout_obj_k03: 92.0\n891\t    attn_last_spatial_k05: 88.8\n892\t    attn_mean_spatial_k05: 91.6\n893\t    attn_rollout_spatial_k05: 92.8\n894\t    attn_last_spatial_k03: 85.6\n895\t    attn_mean_spatial_k03: 90.4\n896\t    attn_last_goal_k05: 98.2\n897\t    attn_mean_goal_k05: 97.4\n898\t    attn_rollout_goal_k05: 96.8\n899\t    attn_last_long_k05: 90.2\n900\t    attn_mean_long_k05: 94.0\n901\t    attn_rollout_long_k05: 94.8\n902\t    attn_last_long_k05_seed43: 90.4\n903\t    attn_mean_long_k05_seed43: 94.6\n904\t    l2norm_obj_k05: 42.6\n905\t    attn_advantage_obj_k05_pp: 56.6\n906\t    l2norm_goal_k05: 59.0\n907\t    attn_advantage_goal_k05_pp: 39.2\n908\t    l2norm_long_k05: 44.6\n909\t    attn_advantage_long_k05_pp: 45.6\n910\t  result_rationale: \"E5 attention pruning 成功的根本原因：attention weights 直接编码了 BART encoder\\\n911\t    \\  创造的 cross-token dependencies。L2norm 失败（特别是在 aggressive compression 下） 是因为 BART\\\n912\t    \\ 使 token norms 近乎 uniform（CV=0.151），导致 L2norm selection  退化为 spatial clustering。而\\\n913\t    \\ attention weights 捕获了 decoder 实际需要哪些 token， 考虑了 cross-token 依赖关系。\\nCross-suite\\\n914\t    \\ 一致性的原因： - Object k=0.5 = 99.2%：简单任务 + attention guidance = near-perfect（仅需保留\\\n915\t    \\ \\n  与 language instruction 相关的 object tokens）\\n- Goal k=0.5 = 98.2%：complex\\\n916\t    \\ task 但 attention 正确识别了 multi-step 所需的 \\n  critical tokens，消除了 task complexity\\\n917\t    \\ amplification\\n- Long k=0.5 = 90.2%：最长 horizon，attention 仍能恢复大部分（vs L2norm 44.6%），\\n\\\n918\t    \\  但 10pp gap vs baseline 来自 long-horizon compounding 的不可完全消除的 information loss\\n\\\n919\t    - Spatial k=0.5 = 88.8-92.8%：spatial tasks 需要 precise spatial token coverage，\\n\\\n920\t    \\  attention 基本正确但不完美\\n\\n\\\"Correct importance metric rescues entangling connectors\\\"\\\n921\t    \\ story： X-VLA L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% vs attention k=0.5 = 99.2% → +56.6pp。 这证明\\\n922\t    \\ pruning failure on entangling connectors 不是因为 information 不可保留， 而是因为 wrong importance\\\n923\t    \\ metric。Attention-based pruning 是 correct metric。\\n\"\n924\t  tables:\n925\t  - title: 'Table: E5 attention pruning vs L2norm on X-VLA (k=0.5, all suites)'\n926\t    columns:\n927\t    - Suite\n928\t    - Baseline\n929\t    - L2norm SR(%)\n930\t    - Random SR(%)\n931\t    - Attn-last SR(%)\n932\t    - Attn-mean SR(%)\n933\t    - Attn advantage vs L2 (pp)\n934\t    data:\n935\t    - - Object\n936\t      - '99.2'\n937\t      - '42.6'\n938\t      - '70.6'\n939\t      - '99.2'\n940\t      - '98.4'\n941\t      - '+56.6'\n942\t    - - Spatial\n943\t      - '93.0'\n944\t      - '58.8'\n945\t      - '71.4'\n946\t      - '88.8'\n947\t      - '91.6'\n948\t      - '+30.0'\n949\t    - - Goal\n950\t      - '98.4'\n951\t      - '59.0'\n952\t      - '67.2'\n953\t      - '98.2'\n954\t      - '97.4'\n955\t      - '+39.2'\n956\t    - - Long\n957\t      - '94.0'\n958\t      - '44.6'\n959\t      - '61.6'\n960\t      - '90.2'\n961\t      - '94.0'\n962\t      - '+45.6'\n963\t  figures_description:\n964\t  - 'Fig: X-VLA pruning method comparison across 4 suites at k=0.5. Three bars per\n965\t    suite (L2norm, random, attention). Attention near-baseline everywhere, L2norm\n966\t    catastrophic on Object/Long.'\n967\t  - 'Fig: Attention advantage heatmap — rows=suites, columns=k values. Color intensity\n968\t    shows pp advantage of attention over L2norm. Hottest zones at aggressive k × complex\n969\t    tasks.'\n970\t  analysis: \"E5 是 best tier 的关键 complementary contribution。它证明： 1. Entangling connectors\\\n971\t    \\ 的 pruning failure 是 metric failure，不是 fundamental limit 2. 正确的 importance metric（attention）can\\\n972\t    \\ rescue X-VLA 至 near-baseline（99.2% at k=0.5） 3. Goal suite 泛化完美（98.2%），确认 assumption\\\n973\t    \\ 5 4. 为 Diagnose-then-Compress framework 增加第三步：Diagnose（CV）→ Choose method \\n\\\n974\t    \\   （attention for low-CV entangling, L2norm for high-CV independent）→ Compress（VTR\\\n975\t    \\ if needed）\\n\\nPaper positioning：§4.7 或 supplementary，作为实用价值的补充。 不改变 primary\\\n976\t    \\ contribution（2-axis framework + CV diagnostic）， 但显著增强 method contribution 的完整性。\\n\"\n977\t- name: Scaling law cross-validation (k=0.5 and k=0.7, 3 models)\n978\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n979\t  description: 'CV-strategy scaling law（Δ(R-L2) monotonically decreasing with CV）在\n980\t    k=0.5 和 k=0.7  已确认，无例外。Final validation 确保 remaining seeds 不引入 exceptions。\n981\t\n982\t    '\n983\t  expected_results:\n984\t    pi05_delta_R_L2_k05: 36.0\n985\t    xvla_delta_R_L2_k05: 26.9\n986\t    openvla_delta_R_L2_k05: -1.8\n987\t    spearman_k05: -1.0\n988\t    pi05_delta_R_L2_k07: 22.2\n989\t    xvla_delta_R_L2_k07: 6.5\n990\t    openvla_delta_R_L2_k07: -5.4\n991\t    spearman_k07: -1.0\n992\t    cv_strategy_abs_spearman: 1.0\n993\t    scaling_law_holds_both_k: true\n994\t    new_exceptions: 0\n995\t  result_rationale: 'Scaling law 在 k=0.5 和 k=0.7 均展示完美的 monotonic pattern（|ρ|=1.0）：\n996\t    CV 越低（tokens 越 uniform），L2norm 越 harmful（因为 uniform distribution 上的  norm-based\n997\t    selection 退化为 spatial clustering），random 越有优势。\n998\t\n999\t    机制链： CV=0.055（π0.5）→ near-uniform importance → L2norm clusters spatially →  catastrophic\n1000\t    coverage loss → +36pp random advantage\n1001\t\n1002\t    CV=0.151（X-VLA）→ moderate uniformity → L2norm partial clustering →  +27pp random\n1003\t    advantage（smaller because BART creates some meaningful differentiation）\n1004\t\n1005\t    CV=0.215（OpenVLA）→ meaningful differentiation → L2norm preserves important tokens\n1006\t    →  -1.8pp（L2norm slightly better, importance-based selection effective）\n1007\t\n1008\t    k=0.7 gap 小于 k=0.5 gap（22.2 vs 36.0 for π0.5）因为 k=0.7 保留更多 tokens， spatial coverage\n1009\t    loss 更轻。但 monotonic ordering 保持不变。\n1010\t\n1011\t    Remaining seeds（已通过 multi-seed 确认）不会引入 exceptions： - π0.5 L2norm k=0.5 dual-seed:\n1012\t    33.4/33.6（std=0.1pp） - X-VLA random k=0.5 tri-seed: 70.6/71.0/69.2（σ=0.9pp） -\n1013\t    Gap reproducibility confirmed across all available seeds。\n1014\t\n1015\t    '\n1016\t  tables:\n1017\t  - title: 'Table: CV-Strategy Scaling Law (dual k validation)'\n1018\t    columns:\n1019\t    - Model\n1020\t    - CV\n1021\t    - Δ(R-L2) k=0.5 (pp)\n1022\t    - Δ(R-L2) k=0.7 (pp)\n1023\t    - Direction\n1024\t    data:\n1025\t    - - pi0.5\n1026\t      - '0.055'\n1027\t      - '+36.0'\n1028\t      - '+22.2'\n1029\t      - Random >> L2norm\n1030\t    - - X-VLA\n1031\t      - '0.151'\n1032\t      - '+26.9'\n1033\t      - '+6.5'\n1034\t      - Random > L2norm\n1035\t    - - OpenVLA\n1036\t      - '0.215'\n1037\t      - '-1.8'\n1038\t      - '-5.4'\n1039\t      - L2norm >= Random\n1040\t    - - SmolVLA\n1041\t      - '0.314'\n1042\t      - N/A (both 0%)\n1043\t      - N/A\n1044\t      - Method-independent\n1045\t  figures_description:\n1046\t  - 'Fig: Scaling law scatter plot — x=CV, y=Δ(R-L2). Two series (k=0.5 solid, k=0.7\n1047\t    dashed). Both monotonically decreasing. Crossover from random-advantage to L2norm-advantage\n1048\t    at CV≈0.2.'\n1049\t  analysis: '|Spearman|=1.0 at both k values 落在 best tier 范围 [0.85, 1.0] 内（实际是上界）。\n1050\t    Scaling law 是 Claim 5 的核心，提供了 practitioner-facing 的 prescriptive guidance： measure\n1051\t    CV → if CV<0.15: use random pruning; if CV>0.2: use L2norm;  if 0.15<CV<0.2: either\n1052\t    method works at mild compression。'\n1053\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"79d91e4c-a5ac-4162-a41b-2935207a2914","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:56:19.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T050917/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '2-axis framework（connector coupling × task complexity）在所有 model×suite\n  组合中得到干净验证。 CV diagnostic 形成完整的连续预测谱（0.038→0.314），scaling law 在 k=0.5 和 k=0.7 均成立且无例外。\n  π0.5 uniformly critical 行为（L2norm 高原 + random cliff）泛化至 Spatial/Goal/Long，机制一致。\n  VTR connector-dependency（pixel-shuffle 有效、MLP 失败）是干净且可解释的结果。 E5 attention pruning\n  在 Goal suite 上完美泛化（SR=96.8-98.2%），为 entangling connector 提供 \"correct importance\n  metric rescues\" 叙事。5 claims 全部保留，reviewer concern RC7 被 4 suites 完全化解。 Paper title\n  不变。叙事核心：Analysis（primary）+ Diagnose-then-Compress method（secondary）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: VTR M-sweep tri-seed completion (SmolVLA)\n  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n  description: 'SmolVLA VTR cross-attention M=16/32/64/96/128 全部 3-seed 完成。 MLP adapter\n    M=32 3-seed 完成。M-curve 平坦性、架构独立性、near-lossless compression 已确认。 剩余工作：最终统计汇总与 paper\n    table 生成。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    m16_3seed_mean_sr: 56.9\n    m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n    m32_3seed_mean_sr: 60.1\n    m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n    m64_3seed_mean_sr: 62.0\n    m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n    m96_3seed_mean_sr: 54.5\n    m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n    m128_3seed_mean_sr: 58.0\n    m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n    mlp_adapter_m32_mean_sr: 63.4\n    mlp_adapter_m32_std: 2.6\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_m128: 0.98\n    m_curve_max_range_pp: 7.5\n    vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n    baseline_sr: 59.2\n  result_rationale: 'M-curve 平坦的根本原因：pixel-shuffle 的空间折叠创造了可逆的 token 纠缠。VTR 的 cross-attention\n    学习了\"展开\"这种纠缠的映射——无论压缩到多少 query token（M=16→128），只要保留足够的 capacity 来表示空间结构，re-encoding\n    就能恢复。M=128 passthrough（58.0%）≈baseline（59.2%）证明 VTR 是恢复而非增强。MLP adapter 与 cross-attention\n    无显著差异（p=0.15）证明任何 learned  re-encoding 都能完成此恢复，不依赖特定架构机制。M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）是统计真实但\n    实际影响有限的波动（54.5% 仍远高于 0% hard pruning）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: SmolVLA VTR M-sweep (3-seed)'\n    columns:\n    - M\n    - Compression\n    - SR mean±std (%)\n    - vs Baseline Δ (pp)\n    - p vs M=128\n    data:\n    - - '16'\n      - 87.5%\n      - 56.9±1.3\n      - '-2.3'\n      - '>0.25'\n    - - '32'\n      - 75%\n      - 60.1±1.3\n      - '+0.9'\n      - '>0.25'\n    - - '64'\n      - 50%\n      - 62.0±2.3\n      - '+2.8'\n      - '>0.25'\n    - - '96'\n      - 25%\n      - 54.5±3.2\n      - '-4.7'\n      - 0.034*\n    - - '128'\n      - 0% (passthrough)\n      - 58.0±3.5\n      - '-1.2'\n      - —\n    - - MLP-adapter@32\n      - 75%\n      - 63.4±2.6\n      - '+4.2'\n      - —\n    - - Hard pruning k=0.5\n      - 50%\n      - '0.0'\n      - '-59.2'\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: M-curve flat plot — x=M (16→128), y=SR(%). Horizontal band at baseline 59.2%±5pp,\n    all M values within band. Hard pruning 0% shown as contrast.'\n  analysis: 'VTR 在 pixel-shuffle connector 上实现 near-lossless compression at ANY ratio（0-87.5%）。\n    这是 Claim 4 的核心证据。M=16 87.5% compression 仅损失 2.3pp，而 hard pruning 在 5% removal  即\n    collapse 至 0%。recovery ratio 0.98 落在 best tier 目标范围 [0.95, 1.05] 内。 架构独立性（VTC\n    vs MLP p=0.15）排除了特定机制假说，支持\"任何 learned re-encoding 均可修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement\"的一般性结论。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — connector-dependent ceiling\n  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n  description: 'VTR M=128 full training 已确认 0% SR（overfitting, 每步输出相同 action）。 VTC-only\n    M=32/M=64 作为 fallback 继续训练。预测结果为 clean negative： VTR 对 MLP projector 无效，VTR ceiling\n    取决于 connector 类型。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    vtconly_m32_sr: 0.0\n    vtconly_m64_sr: 0.0\n    vtconly_m96_sr: 0.0\n    vtr_m128_sr: 0.0\n    openvla_baseline_sr: 74.0\n    failure_mode: overfitting — model outputs identical action per step\n    connector_dependency_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'MLP projector tokens 已经是独立且有意义的（CV=0.215，信息分布在 token 间有分化）。 VTR\n    的 cross-attention 试图将这些已经 well-structured 的 token 重新编码为更少的 query  token，但这个重新编码过程引入了不必要的复杂性。MLP\n    token 的信息是 per-token 局部化的， 与 pixel-shuffle token 的空间纠缠不同——后者的信息恢复 requires 全局\n    re-arrangement， 恰好是 VTR cross-attention 擅长的。对 MLP projector，简单的 hard pruning（k=0.5\n    仍有  37.4% SR）比 VTR 更有效，因为保留的 token 仍然 individually meaningful。VTR 的 22M  额外参数在缺乏\n    spatial entanglement repair 目标时退化为纯噪声拟合器。 所有 M 值（32/64/96/128）均失败进一步证明这不是超参数问题而是架构兼容性问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: VTR connector-dependency summary'\n    columns:\n    - Connector\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Hard prune k=0.5 SR(%)\n    - VTR M=32 SR(%)\n    - VTR Δ vs prune (pp)\n    data:\n    - - Pixel-shuffle\n      - SmolVLA\n      - '0.314'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '60.1'\n      - '+60.1'\n    - - MLP (3-layer)\n      - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - '37.4'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '-37.4'\n    - - Linear+BART\n      - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - 42.6(L2)/70.6(R)\n      - N/A\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: VTR recovery diagram — SmolVLA: 0%→60% (recovery), OpenVLA: 37%→0% (degradation).\n    Visual contrast showing connector-dependent VTR ceiling.'\n  analysis: 'Clean negative result 强化了 paper narrative：VTR 是 pixel-shuffle 的特解而非通用压缩方法。\n    这从 weakness 变为 strength——说明 Diagnose-then-Compress framework 的第一步（CV diagnostic）\n    是必要的，因为不同 connector 需要不同的 compression strategy。MLP projector 应用 simple  pruning（已有\n    graded degradation），pixel-shuffle 应用 VTR re-encoding。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA VTC M-sweep training (M=32/64/96)\n  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n  description: 'OpenVLA VTC-only（无 backbone fine-tuning）M-sweep 训练。此前 M=96_v3 和 M=64_v3  均报\n    failed/negative。预测所有 M 值均无法恢复 SR，与 c4_ext 一致。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    m32_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n    m64_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n    m96_vtconly_sr: 0.0\n    training_loss_converges: true\n    eval_sr_zero: true\n    diagnosis: VTC learns to minimize training loss but does not transfer to closed-loop\n      control\n  result_rationale: 'VTC-only 模式冻结了 backbone，仅训练 22M compressor 参数。对 MLP projector，\n    backbone 已经学习了 per-token semantically meaningful representations。VTC  强制将 256\n    个有独立语义的 token 映射到更少的 query token，丢失了 token-level  semantic granularity。训练 loss\n    收敛（因为 cross-attention 可以学习压缩映射） 但 closed-loop control 失败，因为 action prediction\n    依赖 fine-grained token  discrimination 而非 compressed summary。与 SmolVLA 不同，SmolVLA\n    的 pixel-shuffle  token 本身缺乏 individual semantics（每个 token 编码 32×32 pixel region），\n    VTR re-encoding 只需恢复 spatial structure 而非 semantic content。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '所有 M 值失败构成 c4_ext 的完整 ablation：VTR 的有效性严格绑定到 pixel-shuffle  connector\n    的空间纠缠修复功能。Paper 中作为 §5.3 \"Re-encoding mechanism\" 的 反面证据，说明 VTR 不是通用 token compressor。\n\n    '\n- name: X-VLA cliff threshold 3-seed localization\n  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n  description: 'X-VLA k=0.8 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位已完成。 k=0.80=89.0±0.72pp, k=0.85=67.9±0.31pp。Non-monotonic\n    recovery 确认。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    k080_3seed_mean: 89.0\n    k080_3seed_std: 0.72\n    k085_3seed_mean: 67.9\n    k085_3seed_std: 0.31\n    nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n    cliff_zone: k=0.82-0.87\n    deterministic_sd_below_1pp: true\n  result_rationale: 'BART encoder（12 层 transformer）在 42 tokens（k=0.85）时触发 length-dependent  interaction\n    breakdown。42 tokens 是 BART 自注意力模式的临界密度——低于此密度， BART 的 cross-token mixing 产生的依赖链被截断，导致\n    cascading information loss。 40 tokens（k=0.8）反而恢复，因为 token 密度进一步降低使 BART 退化为  near-independent\n    processing（类似纯 linear projection 行为）。SD<1pp 证明这是  完全 deterministic 的架构属性，非随机效应。3-seed\n    一致性消除了训练 seed 混淆因素。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: X-VLA cliff localization (L2norm, 3-seed)'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Tokens kept\n    - Seed 42\n    - Seed 43\n    - Seed 44\n    - Mean±SD\n    data:\n    - - '0.90'\n      - '45'\n      - '97.6'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '99.4'\n      - 98.4±0.9\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '42'\n      - '68.0'\n      - '67.6'\n      - '68.2'\n      - 67.9±0.3\n    - - '0.80'\n      - '40'\n      - '88.8'\n      - '88.4'\n      - '89.8'\n      - 89.0±0.7\n    - - '0.70'\n      - '35'\n      - '56.2'\n      - '58.2'\n      - '56.4'\n      - 56.9±1.1\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: X-VLA pruning curve with cliff zone highlighted. k=0.85 dip (67.9%) below\n    k=0.8 (89.0%) creating non-monotonic pattern. Error bars from 3-seed.'\n  analysis: 'Cliff 定位精确到 k=0.82-0.87 区间。Non-monotonicity 是 BART encoder 的 emergent  property：存在一个\n    critical token density 使得 BART self-attention 的 cross-token  mixing 恰好最大化 information\n    cascading damage。Paper figure 将此作为  token-entangling connector 的典型特征展示。\n\n    '\n- name: OFT token importance CV measurement\n  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT CV 已从 openvla_entropy_real 和 analysis 中确认为 0.219。 Entropy=0.667≈Standard(0.661)。完成\n    5/5 model diagnostic table。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    oft_cv: 0.219\n    oft_entropy: 0.667\n    standard_openvla_cv: 0.215\n    cv_delta_oft_vs_standard: 0.004\n    entropy_delta: 0.006\n    connector_determines_attention: true\n  result_rationale: 'OFT 与 Standard OpenVLA 共享相同的 3-layer MLP connector（DINOv2+SigLIP\n    fusion  仅增加输入通道但不改变 MLP mixing 结构）。Action head 差异（OFT diffusion vs  Standard autoregressive）不影响\n    vision token attention 分布，因为 attention  pattern 由 connector 在 vision-LLM 接口处决定，action\n    head 在 LLM output 端操作。 CV 0.219≈0.215 差异在 noise level（<0.01），证明 connector 是 attention\n    structure  的唯一决定因素。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Complete 6-model diagnostic spectrum'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Connector\n    - Params\n    - Tokens\n    - Entropy\n    - CV\n    - Pruning Class\n    data:\n    - - pi0\n      - Pure linear\n      - 3.3B\n      - '256'\n      - '0.959'\n      - '0.038'\n      - Immune\n    - - pi0.5\n      - Pure linear (x sqrt_d)\n      - 4B\n      - '768'\n      - ~0.67\n      - '0.055'\n      - Uniformly Critical\n    - - X-VLA\n      - Linear+BART 12L\n      - 880M\n      - '50'\n      - '0.614'\n      - '0.151'\n      - Threshold-graded\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - 3-layer MLP\n      - 7B\n      - '256'\n      - '0.661'\n      - '0.215'\n      - Smooth graded\n    - - OFT\n      - 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\n      - 7B\n      - '512'\n      - '0.667'\n      - '0.219'\n      - Smooth graded (expected)\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - Pixel-shuffle 16x\n      - 450M\n      - '128'\n      - '0.952'\n      - '0.314'\n      - Catastrophic\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '6-model diagnostic table 完整化。CV 连续谱 0.038→0.314 无间断地预测 pruning tolerance。\n    OFT entry 作为 action head 对照实验消除了\"action head 影响 pruning\"的替代假说。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-suite 2-axis framework validation (5 models × 4 suites)\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: '5 models × 4 LIBERO suites × 2 methods（L2norm/random）全矩阵填充。 已收集绝大部分数据。剩余：OpenVLA\n    Spatial random k=0.9, OpenVLA Long L2norm/random k=0.9, 部分 OpenVLA attention cross-suite。预测所有剩余数据点与\n    2-axis framework 一致。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    xvla_object_k09_sr: 97.6\n    xvla_goal_k09_sr: 70.2\n    xvla_long_k09_sr: 27.5\n    xvla_amplification_object_to_goal_pp: 27.4\n    xvla_amplification_object_to_long_pp: 70.1\n    pi05_l2norm_object_k09_sr: 98.2\n    pi05_l2norm_goal_k09_sr: 90.6\n    pi05_l2norm_long_k09_sr: 81.0\n    pi05_amplification_object_to_goal_pp: 7.6\n    pi05_amplification_object_to_long_pp: 17.2\n    openvla_spatial_random_k09_sr: 67.0\n    openvla_long_l2norm_k09_sr: 46.0\n    openvla_long_random_k09_sr: 43.0\n    smolvla_spatial_k095_sr: 0.0\n    smolvla_goal_k095_sr: 0.0\n    smolvla_long_k095_sr: 0.0\n    cross_suite_framework_accuracy_pct: 95\n    axis2_amplification_entangling_min_pp: 27.4\n    axis2_amplification_independent_max_pp: 17.2\n  result_rationale: \"Axis-2（task complexity）放大效应的机制：complex tasks（Goal/Long）要求 multi-step\\\n    \\  reasoning，每一步的 action prediction 依赖前一步保留的 spatial information。 Token-entangling\\\n    \\ connectors（BART/pixel-shuffle）的 pruning damage 在 multi-step  中 compound——单步小损失在序列中累积为大损失。Token-independent\\\n    \\ connectors（linear/MLP） 的 pruning damage 是 per-step 局部的，不会 cascade。\\n具体预测依据：\\\n    \\ - X-VLA Object→Goal 27.4pp 已确认（same k=0.9, same method, only task differs） -\\\n    \\ X-VLA Object→Long 更大（70.1pp）因为 Long 任务平均 horizon 更长，compounding 更严重 - π0.5 L2norm\\\n    \\ Object→Goal 仅 7.6pp（low CV 使得 L2norm 选择的 token 在 spatial \\n  coverage 上已近最优，task\\\n    \\ complexity 无法放大 spatial coverage 的已有优势）\\n- π0.5 Object→Long 17.2pp 稍大，但仍 <20pp（independent\\\n    \\ connector 上限）\\nOpenVLA 剩余预测： - Spatial random k=0.9≈67%：OpenVLA Spatial baseline=80%,\\\n    \\ L2norm k=0.9=75%。\\n  Random 通常比 L2norm 低 5-8pp（CV=0.215 使 L2norm 有轻微优势）\\n- Long\\\n    \\ L2norm k=0.9≈46%：Long baseline=52.8%, 相对保留率≈OpenVLA Object pattern - Long random\\\n    \\ k=0.9≈43%：随机稍差于 L2norm（high CV）\\nSmolVLA 全 suite 0%：pixel-shuffle 纠缠在任何 task\\\n    \\ distribution 下都导致 catastrophic  failure。Spatial/Goal 的 baseline 较低（44.6%/60.8%）不影响\\\n    \\ cliff-edge——即使 baseline  更低，k=0.95 pruning 仍然 collapse 至 0%。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: 2-Axis Framework — Axis-2 amplification at k=0.9 (L2norm)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Connector\n    - Object SR(%)\n    - Spatial SR(%)\n    - Goal SR(%)\n    - Long SR(%)\n    - Amplif O→G (pp)\n    data:\n    - - pi0.5\n      - '0.055'\n      - Linear\n      - '98.2'\n      - '95.0'\n      - '90.6'\n      - '81.0'\n      - '7.6'\n    - - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - Lin+BART\n      - '97.6'\n      - '78.8'\n      - '70.2'\n      - '27.5'\n      - '27.4'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - MLP\n      - '70.6'\n      - '75.0'\n      - '74.8'\n      - '46.0'\n      - -4.2*\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - '0.314'\n      - Pix-shuf\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.0'\n      - N/A\n  - title: 'Table: Cross-suite pruning sensitivity heatmap (SR at k=0.5, random)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    data:\n    - - pi0.5\n      - 69.4 (68.9†)\n      - '71.6'\n      - '73.6'\n      - '46.8'\n    - - X-VLA\n      - 70.6 (70.3†)\n      - '71.4'\n      - 67.9†\n      - '61.6'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '35.8'\n      - ~36\n      - '52.2'\n      - ~35\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.6'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.0'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: 2-axis heatmap — rows=models (sorted by CV), columns=suites (sorted by complexity).\n    Color=SR at k=0.9. Clear gradient: entangling connectors show steep color change\n    across suites, independent connectors show mild change.'\n  - 'Fig: Amplification bar chart — grouped bars per model showing Object→Goal SR\n    drop (pp). X-VLA 27.4pp tower vs π0.5 7.6pp bar. Horizontal line at 20pp separating\n    entangling/independent zones.'\n  analysis: '2-axis framework 在 95% 的 model×suite cells 中正确预测 pruning outcome。 唯一的\n    partial exception：OpenVLA Goal k=0.9 SR（74.8%）高于 Object k=0.9（70.6%）， 但这是 baseline\n    difference（Goal baseline 74.8% = Object baseline 74%），相对  degradation 是一致的。Framework\n    accuracy 95% 落在 best tier 范围 [90, 100] 内。\n\n    Key axis-2 interaction：entangling connectors 放大倍数 27.4pp（X-VLA Object→Goal） 落在\n    best tier 范围 [25, 45] 内。Independent connectors 保持 ≤10pp（π0.5 7.6pp） 符合假设。Long\n    suite 的更大放大（X-VLA 70.1pp, π0.5 17.2pp）与 horizon length  正相关，进一步验证 compounding\n    damage 机制。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR cross-suite generalization (SmolVLA Long)\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M=32 已在 Spatial（53.2%）和 Goal（56.4%）验证。 剩余：Long suite（baseline\n    36.6%）的 VTR recovery。 预测 M=32 Long≈33-38%，完成 Diagnose-then-Compress 全 suite 验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    smolvla_long_baseline_sr: 36.6\n    smolvla_long_hard_prune_k05_sr: 0.0\n    smolvla_long_hard_prune_k095_sr: 0.0\n    vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.5\n    vtr_m32_long_ci95_lower: 31.0\n    vtr_m32_long_ci95_upper: 40.0\n    vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2\n    vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4\n    vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1\n    recovery_ratio_long: 0.97\n    cross_suite_recovery_consistent: true\n  result_rationale: \"VTR cross-suite recovery ratio 预测≈0.97（35.5/36.6）：\\n1. M-curve\\\n    \\ 平坦性在 Object suite 已确认——VTR 的 re-encoding 修复 spatial \\n   entanglement，这是 connector-level\\\n    \\ 属性，与 task distribution 无关。\\n2. Spatial recovery 53.2%/43.8%=1.21 和 Goal recovery\\\n    \\ 56.4%/60.8%=0.93 \\n   显示 cross-suite recovery ratio 围绕 1.0 波动（±20%），中位数 ≈1.0。\\n\\\n    3. Long suite baseline 较低（36.6% vs Object 59.2%）因为 Long 任务本身更难，\\n   但 VTR 不应额外降低——它只修复\\\n    \\ pruning damage，不影响 task difficulty。\\n4. Long 的稍低 recovery（预测 0.97）可能源于 Long\\\n    \\ horizon 放大了 VTR \\n   re-encoding 中的微小信息损失，但效果应 <5pp。\\n\\nVTR 在 Long 上仍将远超 hard\\\n    \\ pruning（35.5% vs 0%），完成全 4 suites 的  \\\"recovery from cliff-edge\\\" 证据链。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: VTR M=32 cross-suite recovery'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline SR(%)\n    - Hard prune k=0.5 SR(%)\n    - VTR M=32 SR(%)\n    - Recovery ratio\n    data:\n    - - Object\n      - '59.2'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '60.1'\n      - '1.015'\n    - - Spatial\n      - 43.8*\n      - '0.6'\n      - '53.2'\n      - 1.21*\n    - - Goal\n      - 60.8*\n      - '0.0'\n      - '56.4'\n      - '0.93'\n    - - Long\n      - '36.6'\n      - '0.0'\n      - 35.5 (pred)\n      - 0.97 (pred)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: VTR recovery bar chart — 4 suites side by side, each showing baseline (gray),\n    hard prune (red, near 0), VTR M=32 (green, near baseline). Consistent recovery\n    pattern across all suites.'\n  analysis: 'VTR cross-suite generalization证明 re-encoding 修复的是 architectural entanglement  而非\n    task-specific information。Recovery ratio ≈1.0 across 4 suites 支持 Claim 4： \"Learned\n    Re-Encoding Achieves Near-Lossless Compression Where Deletion Fails\"。 vtr_smolvla_recovery_ratio\n    0.97 落在 best tier 范围 [0.95, 1.05] 内。\n\n    对 practitioner 的 implication：使用 pixel-shuffle connector 的 VLA 可以通过  VTR 实现任意压缩比而无显著\n    SR 损失。22M 额外参数 + 6% latency overhead 是可接受的代价。\n\n    '\n- name: π0.5 uniformly critical behavior cross-suite validation\n  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n  description: 'π0.5（4B, PaliGemma linear proj）已完成 4 suites baseline + 全面 pruning\n    sweep。 CV=0.055 confirmed。L2norm plateau（k≥0.85 maintains ≥98% Object, ≥88% Spatial/Goal）\n    和 random cliff（k=0.85-0.925 Object collapse）均已 multi-seed 验证。 Scaling law extreme（Δ(R-L2)=+36pp\n    at k=0.5）confirmed。 剩余工作：Cross-suite 一致性最终确认 + paper narrative 整合。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_object: 98.2\n    baseline_spatial: 97.2\n    baseline_goal: 96.4\n    baseline_long: 92.8\n    cv: 0.055\n    l2norm_k095_object: 98.2\n    l2norm_k09_object: 98.2\n    l2norm_k085_object: 98.0\n    l2norm_k095_spatial: 97.8\n    l2norm_k09_spatial: 95.0\n    l2norm_k085_spatial: 88.6\n    l2norm_k095_goal: 90.8\n    l2norm_k09_goal: 90.6\n    l2norm_k085_goal: 88.0\n    l2norm_k095_long: 87.0\n    l2norm_k09_long: 81.0\n    l2norm_k085_long: 78.4\n    random_k095_object: 74.0\n    random_k0925_object: 27.6\n    random_k09_object: 9.0\n    random_k085_object: 5.0\n    random_k095_spatial: 76.4\n    random_k0925_spatial: 58.2\n    random_k09_spatial: 54.6\n    random_k085_spatial: 60.2\n    random_k095_goal: 83.8\n    random_k0925_goal: 70.0\n    random_k09_goal: 62.2\n    random_k085_goal: 52.4\n    random_k095_long: 63.2\n    random_k09_long: 31.8\n    random_k085_long: 45.2\n    l2norm_k05_object: 33.4\n    random_k05_object: 69.4\n    gap_R_minus_L2_k05_pp: 36.0\n    l2norm_k05_spatial: 55.6\n    random_k05_spatial: 71.6\n    gap_spatial_k05_pp: 16.0\n    l2norm_k05_goal: 59.8\n    random_k05_goal: 73.6\n    gap_goal_k05_pp: 13.8\n    l2norm_k05_long: 50.2\n    random_k05_long: 46.8\n    gap_long_k05_pp: -3.4\n  result_rationale: \"π0.5 \\\"uniformly critical\\\" 行为的 cross-suite 一致性验证了 Claim 1 和\\\n    \\ Claim 5：\\n1. **L2norm plateau 跨 suite 一致**：k≥0.85 时 L2norm 在所有 4 suites 维持高\\\n    \\ SR\\n   （Object 98%, Spatial 88.6%, Goal 88%, Long 78.4%）。Plateau 随 task complexity\\\n    \\ \\n   轻微下降但保持>78%。机制：L2norm 的 deterministic selection 保留 spatial coverage，\\n\\\n    \\   low CV（0.055）使选中的 token subset 具有 near-uniform importance，覆盖度好。\\n\\n2. **Random\\\n    \\ cliff 跨 suite 差异化**：\\n   - Object cliff dramatic（74→28→9→5%），因为 Object tasks\\\n    \\ 有 concentrated critical \\n     tokens（object identity discrimination 依赖 specific\\\n    \\ patches）\\n   - Spatial cliff milder（76→58→55→60%），因为 spatial layout information\\\n    \\ 是 \\n     distributed 的，random removal 不会完全摧毁 spatial signal\\n   - Goal cliff\\\n    \\ moderate（84→70→62→52%），因为 Goal tasks 混合了 spatial 和 \\n     semantic disambiguation\\n\\\n    \\   - Long cliff steep（63→32→45%），因为 long-horizon compounding 放大了 random \\n  \\\n    \\   token loss\\n\\n3. **Scaling law（Δ(R-L2)）cross-suite 演变**：\\n   - Object k=0.5:\\\n    \\ +36.0pp（random wins massively, extreme of scaling law）\\n   - Spatial k=0.5:\\\n    \\ +16.0pp（random wins, spatial distributed info helps random）\\n   - Goal k=0.5:\\\n    \\ +13.8pp（random wins, similar to spatial）\\n   - Long k=0.5: -3.4pp（L2norm slightly\\\n    \\ wins — long horizon 使 L2norm 的 \\n     deterministic consistency 成为优势，random\\\n    \\ 的 per-step variance compounds）\\n   \\n   Gap 从 +36→+16→+14→-3.4 的变化不违反 scaling\\\n    \\ law：scaling law 是 \\n   cross-model（CV drives direction），不是 cross-suite。Suite\\\n    \\ 影响 gap \\n   magnitude 但不改变 sign（除 Long 的轻微 reversal，可解释为 horizon effect）。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: π0.5 L2norm plateau cross-suite'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    data:\n    - - 1.0 (baseline)\n      - '98.2'\n      - '97.2'\n      - '96.4'\n      - '92.8'\n    - - '0.95'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '97.8'\n      - '90.8'\n      - '87.0'\n    - - '0.925'\n      - '99.2'\n      - '97.0'\n      - '89.8'\n      - —\n    - - '0.9'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '95.0'\n      - '90.6'\n      - '81.0'\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '98.0'\n      - '88.6'\n      - '88.0'\n      - '78.4'\n    - - '0.7'\n      - '55.0'\n      - '67.0'\n      - '73.6'\n      - '62.6'\n    - - '0.5'\n      - '33.4'\n      - '55.6'\n      - '59.8'\n      - '50.2'\n    - - '0.3'\n      - '51.0'\n      - '57.2'\n      - '50.6'\n      - '36.6'\n  - title: 'Table: π0.5 random cliff cross-suite'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    data:\n    - - '0.95'\n      - '74.0'\n      - '76.4'\n      - '83.8'\n      - '63.2'\n    - - '0.925'\n      - '27.6'\n      - '58.2'\n      - '70.0'\n      - —\n    - - '0.9'\n      - '9.0'\n      - '54.6'\n      - '62.2'\n      - '31.8'\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '5.0'\n      - '60.2'\n      - '52.4'\n      - '45.2'\n    - - '0.7'\n      - '75.5'\n      - '74.4'\n      - '75.6'\n      - '65.8'\n    - - '0.5'\n      - '69.4'\n      - '71.6'\n      - '73.6'\n      - '46.8'\n    - - '0.3'\n      - '36.4'\n      - '43.4'\n      - '52.8'\n      - '29.6'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: π0.5 L2norm vs random pruning curves, 4 suites side-by-side. L2norm plateau\n    vs random cliff contrast. Object cliff most dramatic, Spatial most resilient.'\n  - 'Fig: Concentrated vs distributed critical tokens illustration — Object tasks\n    show localized critical patches, Spatial tasks show diffuse importance.'\n  analysis: 'π0.5 完整 cross-suite 数据确认了核心假设 3：uniformly critical behavior  generalize\n    至 Spatial/Goal，且机制一致（concentrated vs distributed critical tokens  决定 cliff severity）。pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp=36.0pp\n    落在 best tier  范围 [30, 40] 内。\n\n    π0.5 是 scaling law 的 extreme point（CV=0.055, 最低），在所有 suite 上都展现 L2norm catastrophic\n    failure at aggressive compression。这强化了 \"CV predicts optimal  pruning strategy\"\n    narrative——对 low-CV models，importance-based pruning actively harmful。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA-OFT graded degradation cross-suite validation\n  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n  description: 'OFT（7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fusion, 512 tokens）在兼容硬件（A100+torch2.2）\n    上进行 4 suites baseline + pruning 评估。CV=0.219≈OpenVLA(0.215) 预测相同的  graded degradation\n    模式。此实验验证 action head（OFT vs Standard）不影响 pruning behavior。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_object: 97.0\n    baseline_spatial: 95.0\n    baseline_goal: 96.0\n    baseline_long: 85.0\n    l2norm_k095_object: 91.0\n    l2norm_k09_object: 83.0\n    l2norm_k07_object: 65.0\n    l2norm_k05_object: 50.0\n    l2norm_k03_object: 28.0\n    random_k095_object: 90.0\n    random_k09_object: 80.0\n    random_k07_object: 60.0\n    random_k05_object: 46.0\n    random_k03_object: 25.0\n    gap_R_minus_L2_k05_object_pp: -4.0\n    gap_R_minus_L2_k07_object_pp: -5.0\n    l2norm_k09_spatial: 82.0\n    l2norm_k09_goal: 84.0\n    l2norm_k09_long: 68.0\n    cv: 0.219\n    entropy: 0.667\n  result_rationale: \"OFT 使用与 Standard OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector。CV 0.219≈0.215\\\n    \\ 的高度一致性 预测几乎相同的 pruning degradation pattern：\\n1. **Graded degradation 预测**：OpenVLA\\\n    \\ relative retention at k=0.5 = 37.4/74 = 50.5%。\\n   OFT baseline 更高（~97%），absolute\\\n    \\ SR 更高但 relative pattern 一致。\\n   预测 OFT k=0.5 L2norm ≈ 97×0.515 ≈ 50%。\\n\\n2.\\\n    \\ **L2norm > random 一致**：high CV（0.219）= meaningful importance differentiation\\\n    \\ → \\n   L2norm selection effective。预测 L2norm 在所有 k 值优于 random 3-6pp，\\n   与 OpenVLA\\\n    \\ pattern（+1.4 to +5.4pp）一致。\\n\\n3. **Cross-suite pattern**：OFT 的 512 tokens（vs\\\n    \\ OpenVLA 256）提供更高的信息冗余，\\n   可能使 pruning tolerance 略高于 OpenVLA。但 connector mechanism\\\n    \\ 相同，\\n   degradation shape 应一致（smooth graded）。\\n\\n4. **Action head 独立性**：OFT\\\n    \\ diffusion action head 和 Standard autoregressive \\n   action head 对 pruning 的反应应\\\n    \\ identical，因为 pruning 发生在 vision-LLM \\n   接口而非 action decode 阶段。这是 connector-determines-pruning\\\n    \\ 假说的关键证据。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: OFT vs OpenVLA pruning comparison (Object suite, L2norm)'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - OFT SR(%) (pred)\n    - OpenVLA SR(%)\n    - OFT retention\n    - OpenVLA retention\n    data:\n    - - '1.0'\n      - '97.0'\n      - '74.0'\n      - 100%\n      - 100%\n    - - '0.95'\n      - '91.0'\n      - '69.4'\n      - 93.8%\n      - 93.8%\n    - - '0.9'\n      - '83.0'\n      - '62.0'\n      - 85.6%\n      - 83.8%\n    - - '0.7'\n      - '65.0'\n      - '49.0'\n      - 67.0%\n      - 66.2%\n    - - '0.5'\n      - '50.0'\n      - '37.4'\n      - 51.5%\n      - 50.5%\n    - - '0.3'\n      - '28.0'\n      - '20.6'\n      - 28.9%\n      - 27.8%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: OFT vs OpenVLA pruning curves overlaid, normalized by baseline. Near-identical\n    relative degradation pattern despite different baselines and action heads.'\n  analysis: 'OFT 实验是 paper 中消除 confound 的关键 ablation：same connector + different action\n    head  → same pruning behavior，证明 connector 是 causal factor。如果 Blackwell GPU  兼容性问题无法解决，OFT\n    可以仅通过 CV/entropy analysis（已完成）纳入 paper， 辅以 official baseline 引用。LIBERO eval 是\n    bonus（icing on the cake）， CV/entropy 已足够支持 Claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Perceiver Resampler connector fine-tune + pruning\n  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n  description: 'RoboFlamingo（Perceiver Resampler: 64 learned query tokens 通过 cross-attention  attend\n    to vision patches）在 LIBERO Object 上 fine-tune 后进行 pruning sweep。 验证第 4 种 connector\n    family 的 pruning behavior。此前训练尝试因基础设施问题被 kill。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_object_sr: 58.0\n    baseline_ci95:\n    - 53.5\n    - 62.4\n    l2norm_k095_sr: 52.0\n    l2norm_k09_sr: 42.0\n    l2norm_k07_sr: 22.0\n    l2norm_k05_sr: 10.0\n    random_k095_sr: 50.0\n    random_k09_sr: 38.0\n    random_k07_sr: 18.0\n    random_k05_sr: 8.0\n    importance_cv: 0.22\n    entropy_ratio: 0.82\n    connector_class: token-entangling (cross-attention)\n    pruning_pattern: steep graded → threshold at k≈0.7\n  result_rationale: \"Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 机制创造了中等程度的 token entanglement：\\n\\\n    1. **Entanglement 机制**：64 query tokens 各自通过 cross-attention attend 全部 vision \\n\\\n    \\   patches。每个 output token 不再对应特定 spatial region（unlike linear proj），\\n   而是\\\n    \\ learned mixture of all patches。但与 pixel-shuffle 不同，这种 mixture \\n   是 learned\\\n    \\ 的且 query-specific，因此不同 query 可能 specialize to different \\n   spatial/semantic\\\n    \\ aspects。\\n\\n2. **CV 预测 ~0.22**：介于 X-VLA（0.151）和 SmolVLA（0.314）之间。\\n   Cross-attention\\\n    \\ 创造的依赖比 BART sequential mixing 更直接但不如 pixel-shuffle \\n   的空间折叠极端。Query specialization\\\n    \\ 产生 moderate importance heterogeneity。\\n\\n3. **Pruning pattern 预测**：steep graded\\\n    \\ degradation。k=0.95 开始可见 drop \\n   （~10% relative），k=0.7 显著下降（~60% relative），k=0.5\\\n    \\ 接近 collapse。\\n   比 OpenVLA/MLP 更陡但不如 SmolVLA/pixel-shuffle catastrophic。\\n\\n\\\n    4. **Baseline 预测 ~58%**：first-attempt fine-tuning on LIBERO，\\n   RoboFlamingo\\\n    \\ original architecture 不是为 LIBERO 任务优化的。\\n   合理的 mid-range SR。\\n\\n5. **L2norm\\\n    \\ ≈ random**：CV ~0.22 处于 L2norm 和 random 的交叉区域，\\n   两种方法差异应 <5pp，类似 OpenVLA pattern。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Perceiver Resampler pruning curve (predicted)'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Tokens kept\n    - L2norm SR(%)\n    - Random SR(%)\n    - Δ(R-L2)\n    data:\n    - - '1.0'\n      - '64'\n      - '58.0'\n      - '58.0'\n      - '0'\n    - - '0.95'\n      - '61'\n      - '52.0'\n      - '50.0'\n      - '-2.0'\n    - - '0.9'\n      - '58'\n      - '42.0'\n      - '38.0'\n      - '-4.0'\n    - - '0.7'\n      - '45'\n      - '22.0'\n      - '18.0'\n      - '-4.0'\n    - - '0.5'\n      - '32'\n      - '10.0'\n      - '8.0'\n      - '-2.0'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: 4-connector family pruning curves on same axes — Linear (π0.5, flat), MLP\n    (OpenVLA, gradual), Perceiver (RoboFlamingo, steep graded), Pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA,\n    cliff). Continuous spectrum of pruning tolerance.'\n  analysis: 'Perceiver Resampler 填补了 connector spectrum 的空白——在 MLP（graded）和 pixel-shuffle  （catastrophic）之间提供了第\n    4 个 data point。如果 CV ~0.22 且 pruning pattern  呈 steep graded，它将进一步验证 CV 作为 continuous\n    predictor 的有效性。\n\n    对 paper 的贡献：从 3 connector families 扩展到 4，增加了 paper 的 generalizability。 但即使此实验因基础设施问题未完成，paper\n    已有 5 models × 3 families 的充分覆盖， Perceiver 可作为 future work 提及。在 best tier 下，此实验成功完成并增加\n    paper  的 reviewer 说服力。\n\n    '\n- name: E5 attention-based pruning — correct importance metric for entangling connectors\n  plan_id: e5_attention_pruning_xvla\n  description: 'X-VLA attention-based token pruning（last-layer / mean / rollout）在\n    4 suites 上验证。 核心发现：attention-based importance 在 entangling connector 上远优于 L2norm，\n    因为 attention 捕获了 BART encoder 创造的 cross-token dependencies。 已有数据覆盖 Object/Spatial/Goal/Long\n    at k=0.5 和 k=0.3/k=0.7 部分点。 Goal suite 泛化已确认（SR=96.8-98.2% at k=0.5）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    attn_last_obj_k05: 99.2\n    attn_mean_obj_k05: 98.4\n    attn_rollout_obj_k05: 97.4\n    attn_last_obj_k07: 99.2\n    attn_last_obj_k03: 84.2\n    attn_mean_obj_k03: 96.0\n    attn_rollout_obj_k03: 92.0\n    attn_last_spatial_k05: 88.8\n    attn_mean_spatial_k05: 91.6\n    attn_rollout_spatial_k05: 92.8\n    attn_last_spatial_k03: 85.6\n    attn_mean_spatial_k03: 90.4\n    attn_last_goal_k05: 98.2\n    attn_mean_goal_k05: 97.4\n    attn_rollout_goal_k05: 96.8\n    attn_last_long_k05: 90.2\n    attn_mean_long_k05: 94.0\n    attn_rollout_long_k05: 94.8\n    attn_last_long_k05_seed43: 90.4\n    attn_mean_long_k05_seed43: 94.6\n    l2norm_obj_k05: 42.6\n    attn_advantage_obj_k05_pp: 56.6\n    l2norm_goal_k05: 59.0\n    attn_advantage_goal_k05_pp: 39.2\n    l2norm_long_k05: 44.6\n    attn_advantage_long_k05_pp: 45.6\n  result_rationale: \"E5 attention pruning 成功的根本原因：attention weights 直接编码了 BART encoder\\\n    \\  创造的 cross-token dependencies。L2norm 失败（特别是在 aggressive compression 下） 是因为 BART\\\n    \\ 使 token norms 近乎 uniform（CV=0.151），导致 L2norm selection  退化为 spatial clustering。而\\\n    \\ attention weights 捕获了 decoder 实际需要哪些 token， 考虑了 cross-token 依赖关系。\\nCross-suite\\\n    \\ 一致性的原因： - Object k=0.5 = 99.2%：简单任务 + attention guidance = near-perfect（仅需保留\\\n    \\ \\n  与 language instruction 相关的 object tokens）\\n- Goal k=0.5 = 98.2%：complex\\\n    \\ task 但 attention 正确识别了 multi-step 所需的 \\n  critical tokens，消除了 task complexity\\\n    \\ amplification\\n- Long k=0.5 = 90.2%：最长 horizon，attention 仍能恢复大部分（vs L2norm 44.6%），\\n\\\n    \\  但 10pp gap vs baseline 来自 long-horizon compounding 的不可完全消除的 information loss\\n\\\n    - Spatial k=0.5 = 88.8-92.8%：spatial tasks 需要 precise spatial token coverage，\\n\\\n    \\  attention 基本正确但不完美\\n\\n\\\"Correct importance metric rescues entangling connectors\\\"\\\n    \\ story： X-VLA L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% vs attention k=0.5 = 99.2% → +56.6pp。 这证明\\\n    \\ pruning failure on entangling connectors 不是因为 information 不可保留， 而是因为 wrong importance\\\n    \\ metric。Attention-based pruning 是 correct metric。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: E5 attention pruning vs L2norm on X-VLA (k=0.5, all suites)'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline\n    - L2norm SR(%)\n    - Random SR(%)\n    - Attn-last SR(%)\n    - Attn-mean SR(%)\n    - Attn advantage vs L2 (pp)\n    data:\n    - - Object\n      - '99.2'\n      - '42.6'\n      - '70.6'\n      - '99.2'\n      - '98.4'\n      - '+56.6'\n    - - Spatial\n      - '93.0'\n      - '58.8'\n      - '71.4'\n      - '88.8'\n      - '91.6'\n      - '+30.0'\n    - - Goal\n      - '98.4'\n      - '59.0'\n      - '67.2'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '97.4'\n      - '+39.2'\n    - - Long\n      - '94.0'\n      - '44.6'\n      - '61.6'\n      - '90.2'\n      - '94.0'\n      - '+45.6'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: X-VLA pruning method comparison across 4 suites at k=0.5. Three bars per\n    suite (L2norm, random, attention). Attention near-baseline everywhere, L2norm\n    catastrophic on Object/Long.'\n  - 'Fig: Attention advantage heatmap — rows=suites, columns=k values. Color intensity\n    shows pp advantage of attention over L2norm. Hottest zones at aggressive k × complex\n    tasks.'\n  analysis: \"E5 是 best tier 的关键 complementary contribution。它证明： 1. Entangling connectors\\\n    \\ 的 pruning failure 是 metric failure，不是 fundamental limit 2. 正确的 importance metric（attention）can\\\n    \\ rescue X-VLA 至 near-baseline（99.2% at k=0.5） 3. Goal suite 泛化完美（98.2%），确认 assumption\\\n    \\ 5 4. 为 Diagnose-then-Compress framework 增加第三步：Diagnose（CV）→ Choose method \\n\\\n    \\   （attention for low-CV entangling, L2norm for high-CV independent）→ Compress（VTR\\\n    \\ if needed）\\n\\nPaper positioning：§4.7 或 supplementary，作为实用价值的补充。 不改变 primary\\\n    \\ contribution（2-axis framework + CV diagnostic）， 但显著增强 method contribution 的完整性。\\n\"\n- name: Scaling law cross-validation (k=0.5 and k=0.7, 3 models)\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: 'CV-strategy scaling law（Δ(R-L2) monotonically decreasing with CV）在\n    k=0.5 和 k=0.7  已确认，无例外。Final validation 确保 remaining seeds 不引入 exceptions。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pi05_delta_R_L2_k05: 36.0\n    xvla_delta_R_L2_k05: 26.9\n    openvla_delta_R_L2_k05: -1.8\n    spearman_k05: -1.0\n    pi05_delta_R_L2_k07: 22.2\n    xvla_delta_R_L2_k07: 6.5\n    openvla_delta_R_L2_k07: -5.4\n    spearman_k07: -1.0\n    cv_strategy_abs_spearman: 1.0\n    scaling_law_holds_both_k: true\n    new_exceptions: 0\n  result_rationale: 'Scaling law 在 k=0.5 和 k=0.7 均展示完美的 monotonic pattern（|ρ|=1.0）：\n    CV 越低（tokens 越 uniform），L2norm 越 harmful（因为 uniform distribution 上的  norm-based\n    selection 退化为 spatial clustering），random 越有优势。\n\n    机制链： CV=0.055（π0.5）→ near-uniform importance → L2norm clusters spatially →  catastrophic\n    coverage loss → +36pp random advantage\n\n    CV=0.151（X-VLA）→ moderate uniformity → L2norm partial clustering →  +27pp random\n    advantage（smaller because BART creates some meaningful differentiation）\n\n    CV=0.215（OpenVLA）→ meaningful differentiation → L2norm preserves important tokens\n    →  -1.8pp（L2norm slightly better, importance-based selection effective）\n\n    k=0.7 gap 小于 k=0.5 gap（22.2 vs 36.0 for π0.5）因为 k=0.7 保留更多 tokens， spatial coverage\n    loss 更轻。但 monotonic ordering 保持不变。\n\n    Remaining seeds（已通过 multi-seed 确认）不会引入 exceptions： - π0.5 L2norm k=0.5 dual-seed:\n    33.4/33.6（std=0.1pp） - X-VLA random k=0.5 tri-seed: 70.6/71.0/69.2（σ=0.9pp） -\n    Gap reproducibility confirmed across all available seeds。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: CV-Strategy Scaling Law (dual k validation)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Δ(R-L2) k=0.5 (pp)\n    - Δ(R-L2) k=0.7 (pp)\n    - Direction\n    data:\n    - - pi0.5\n      - '0.055'\n      - '+36.0'\n      - '+22.2'\n      - Random >> L2norm\n    - - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - '+26.9'\n      - '+6.5'\n      - Random > L2norm\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - '-1.8'\n      - '-5.4'\n      - L2norm >= Random\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - '0.314'\n      - N/A (both 0%)\n      - N/A\n      - Method-independent\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scaling law scatter plot — x=CV, y=Δ(R-L2). Two series (k=0.5 solid, k=0.7\n    dashed). Both monotonically decreasing. Crossover from random-advantage to L2norm-advantage\n    at CV≈0.2.'\n  analysis: '|Spearman|=1.0 at both k values 落在 best tier 范围 [0.85, 1.0] 内（实际是上界）。\n    Scaling law 是 Claim 5 的核心，提供了 practitioner-facing 的 prescriptive guidance： measure\n    CV → if CV<0.15: use random pruning; if CV>0.2: use L2norm;  if 0.15<CV<0.2: either\n    method works at mild compression。'\n","numLines":1053,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1053}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HkXpUgPuedL8BmGWBNY3aQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nI found some information about CoRL 2026, though the search results don't contain a dedicated page with the complete reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information:\n\nFrom the CoRL 2026 website, the aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\nThe search results show that all submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nFor more detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifics, the most relevant resource would be:\n- **OpenReview Platform**: Papers may be submitted through OpenReview via the link here (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) - the review form and detailed reviewer guidelines are typically hosted on this platform.\n\nFor comparison, I found that CoRL 2023 had detailed reviewer guidelines available, which included review criteria focusing on relevance, novelty, and limitations. However, the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form appear to be available directly through the OpenReview platform linked above.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"03fd9a28-411a-4041-b229-daff2b5b9d79","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:56:21.334Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LG5QdmA9eH2nwJvYs6WX71","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"I found some information about CoRL 2026, though the search results don't contain a dedicated page with the complete reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information:\n\nFrom the CoRL 2026 website, the aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\nThe search results show that all submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nFor more detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifics, the most relevant resource would be:\n- **OpenReview Platform**: Papers may be submitted through OpenReview via the link here (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) - the review form and detailed reviewer guidelines are typically hosted on this platform.\n\nFor comparison, I found that CoRL 2023 had detailed reviewer guidelines available, which included review criteria focusing on relevance, novelty, and limitations. However, the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form appear to be available directly through the OpenReview platform linked above."],"durationSeconds":5.900231336000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01APfNrzcmQkK1Cj3bg6tZJG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond Paper-to-Paper: Structured Profiling and Rubric Scoring for Paper-Reviewer Matching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.05866\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/\"}]\n\nThe search returned results for NeurIPS 2025 and ICLR 2025 reviewer guidelines, as well as a CoRL 2024 page, but not specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with a scoring rubric. Let me search more specifically for CoRL 2025.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"RemembeRL - Workshop @ CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://rememberl-corl25.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information from CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 (as well as references to CoRL 2026), but I was unable to locate a dedicated page with specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric. The OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 exists but doesn't show detailed content in the search results.\n\nHowever, I can share what I found:\n\n**For CoRL 2024**, submissions were evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n**For CoRL 2023**, the reviewer guidelines included evaluation of several key criteria: Originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work. More specifically:\n\n- Originality: Whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and if related work is adequately cited\n\n- Quality: Whether the submission is technically sound, claims are well supported (by theoretical analysis or experimental results), methods are appropriate, and if this is complete work or work in progress\n\n- Clarity: Whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader\n\nTo access the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric, I recommend visiting the OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Conference or checking the official CoRL website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"1309bc83-5872-40e4-8ba2-16a120eb499f","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:56:25.151Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01T3ApYzMWifAb7S4MZLvQif","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/"},{"title":"Beyond Paper-to-Paper: Structured Profiling and Rubric Scoring for Paper-Reviewer Matching","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.05866"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/"}]},"The search returned results for NeurIPS 2025 and ICLR 2025 reviewer guidelines, as well as a CoRL 2024 page, but not specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with a scoring rubric. Let me search more specifically for CoRL 2025.",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014MjevaZCftnmqEXN193f7E","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"RemembeRL - Workshop @ CoRL 2025","url":"https://rememberl-corl25.github.io/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found information from CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 (as well as references to CoRL 2026), but I was unable to locate a dedicated page with specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric. The OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 exists but doesn't show detailed content in the search results.\n\nHowever, I can share what I found:\n\n**For CoRL 2024**, submissions were evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n**For CoRL 2023**, the reviewer guidelines included evaluation of several key criteria: Originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work. More specifically:\n\n- Originality: Whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and if related work is adequately cited\n\n- Quality: Whether the submission is technically sound, claims are well supported (by theoretical analysis or experimental results), methods are appropriate, and if this is complete work or work in progress\n\n- Clarity: Whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader\n\nTo access the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric, I recommend visiting the OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Conference or checking the official CoRL website."],"durationSeconds":9.244702904000002}}
