{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ai2qD5AfT84FHUyAbsagjE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring criteria rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found:\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, and ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\nHowever, the search results from the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page do not include specific information about the numerical rating scale or scoring criteria details for reviewers. The page content appears to be incomplete in the search results. You may need to visit the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews directly to see the complete reviewer scoring scale information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"41f69269-73c0-493d-831c-e4f035258144","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:56:41.268Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring criteria rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013vCkxEGbuEpRYbB5oxND2y","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found:\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, and ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\nHowever, the search results from the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page do not include specific information about the numerical rating scale or scoring criteria details for reviewers. The page content appears to be incomplete in the search results. You may need to visit the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews directly to see the complete reviewer scoring scale information."],"durationSeconds":6.617332460000005}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HaJ6UouDDSgvLRtSW4uGur","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale 1-10 acceptance criteria originality quality\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965318/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here's what the official guidelines specify:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work, with originality assessed by asking \"Are the problems or methods new?\"\n\nRegarding the review process more broadly, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nThe search results from the official CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page indicate the key evaluation criteria but do not include specific details about a 1-10 rating scale or explicit acceptance thresholds. The guidelines emphasize constructive, evidence-based feedback rather than focusing on a numerical scale. If you need more specific information about the exact rating scale used, that information may be contained in other sections of the full reviewer guidelines document.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"99c241c6-3049-4a4a-a2f0-707111c19433","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:56:41.782Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale 1-10 acceptance criteria originality quality","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YX3JbMi7S1EmJFcwdUyFBs","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965318/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here's what the official guidelines specify:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work, with originality assessed by asking \"Are the problems or methods new?\"\n\nRegarding the review process more broadly, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nThe search results from the official CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page indicate the key evaluation criteria but do not include specific details about a 1-10 rating scale or explicit acceptance thresholds. The guidelines emphasize constructive, evidence-based feedback rather than focusing on a numerical scale. If you need more specific information about the exact rating scale used, that information may be contained in other sections of the full reviewer guidelines document."],"durationSeconds":6.628321175999997}}
