{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KhDpM96c8HTAm9xTcqvjZj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've done enough searching. Based on my research:\n\n- CoRL uses OpenReview\n- CoRL 2023 used a scale with a range of roughly 4.70-10.00, suggesting a 1-10 scale\n- CoRL 2024 used a scale with a range of roughly 1.70-4.00, suggesting possibly a different scale\n- The acceptance rate for CoRL 2024 was ~39%\n- CoRL evaluates: originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance, limitations\n\nFor the review, I'll use a standard robotics/ML conference review format. Based on the CoRL 2023 guidelines (which were more detailed), the review dimensions are:\n\n\n1. Originality\n2. Quality\n3. Clarity\n4. Significance\n5. Relevance\n\nI'll use a 1-10 scale similar to what was used in CoRL 2023, with strong reject at 1-3, reject at 4, borderline reject at 5, borderline accept at 6, accept at 7, strong accept at 8, and outstanding at 9-10. Now I'll structure the review by evaluating the methods and experiments first, then the novelty and related work in parallel, before synthesizing everything into a final assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":78404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":385},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"32e2356f-47e2-4a8a-9104-b37f927c78b5"}
