OpenVLA VTC M-sweep (M=32/64/96)\n- All M values: 0% SR. Training loss converges but doesn't transfer to closed-loop control.\n\n### E4: X-VLA cliff threshold (3-seed)\n- k=0.80: 89.0±0.72pp, k=0.85: 67.9±0.31pp. Non-monotonic, SD<1pp → deterministic.\n\n### E5: OFT CV measurement\n- OFT CV=0.219, OpenVLA CV=0.215. Delta=0.004. Action head doesn't affect pruning.\n\n### E6: Cross-suite 2-axis validation (5 models × 4 suites)\n- Framework accuracy 95%. X-VLA amplification Object→Goal: 27.4pp. π0.5 only 7.6pp.\n- Entangling connectors ≥27pp amplification, independent ≤10pp.\n\n### E7: VTR cross-suite generalization\n- Object: recovery ratio 1.015, Spatial: 1.21, Goal: 0.93, Long: 0.97 (predicted)\n\n### E8: π0.5 uniformly critical behavior\n- L2norm plateau (k≥0.85): Object 98%, Spatial 88.6%, Goal 88%, Long 78.4%\n- Random cliff: Object 74→28→9→5% at k=0.95→0.925→0.9→0.85\n- Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5: +36pp (Object), +16pp (Spatial), +13.8pp (Goal), -3.4pp (Long)\n\n### E9: Attention-based pruning (X-VLA)\n- Attn-last Object k=0.5: 99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → +56.6pp\n- Goal k=0.5: 98.2% (+39.2pp), Long k=0.5: 90.2% (+45.6pp)\n- At k=0.3: attn-mean 96.0% Object, 90.4% Spatial\n\n### E10: Scaling law\n- Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5: π0.5 +36, X-VLA +26.9, OpenVLA -1.8. |ρ|=1.0 Spearman at both k=0.5 and k=0.7.\n\n### E11: Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo)\n- CV≈0.22. Steep graded degradation. L2norm slightly better than random.\n- Baseline 58%, k=0.5: L2norm 10%, Random 8%.\n\n### E12: OFT graded degradation\n- Baseline ~97% Object. k=0.5 L2norm: 50%. Relative retention matches OpenVLA within 2pp.\n\n## Experiments NOT in Paper (from YAML)\n- VTR Long suite result (35.5% predicted, recovery ratio 0.97) — listed as predicted, may not be run\n- OFT full cross-suite pruning sweep — only partial results shown in paper\n- Perceiver Resampler results appear to be predicted/estimated rather than fully run\n\n## YOUR TASK\n\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Experimental Methodology**\n   - Is the experimental setup sound? Controls adequate?\n   - Are the evaluation metrics appropriate (SR on LIBERO)?\n   - Is the number of seeds sufficient? Statistical rigor?\n   - Any methodological gaps?\n\n2. **Results Analysis**\n   - Are claims well-supported by evidence?\n   - Any overclaimed results?\n   - Missing baselines or comparisons?\n   - Non-monotonic behaviors (π0.5 random, X-VLA cliff) — adequately explained?\n\n3. **VTR Method**\n   - Is the method well-motivated?\n   - Is the evaluation fair? Missing comparisons to other compression methods?\n   - 22M parameters + training cost — discussed adequately?\n\n4. **Reproducibility**\n   - Are implementation details sufficient?\n   - Can the experiments be reproduced?\n\n5. **Weaknesses**\n   - What are the main methodological weaknesses?\n   - Any concerns about cherry-picking or selective reporting?\n\nProvide scores for: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance. Then an overall score (1-10) with justification. List 3-5 main strengths and 3-5 main weaknesses. Format as a structured review.","uuid":"3e7e825d-4870-476f-88df-187e7a3edb96","session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## CoRL Review Criteria\nCoRL evaluates: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance to robot learning, Limitations. Scale: 1-10 (1-3 reject, 4-5 borderline reject, 6 borderline accept, 7 accept, 8 strong accept, 9-10 outstanding). Acceptance rate ~39%.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n\nThe paper presents a systematic study of vision token pruning across 6 VLA models (π0, π0.5, X-VLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, SmolVLA + RoboFlamingo), 4 connector families, and 4 LIBERO task suites. Key contributions:\n1. 2-axis framework: token coupling (connector architecture) × task complexity → pruning robustness\n2. Importance CV as zero-cost diagnostic (0.038→0.314 spectrum) predicting pruning tolerance and optimal strategy\n3. Pixel-shuffle creates irreversible token entanglement (0% SR at 5% removal)\n4. VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) achieves near-lossless compression (0–87.5%) where deletion fails\n5. Attention-based pruning rescues entangling connectors (+56.6pp over L2-norm on X-VLA)\n\n## Detailed Experimental Results (from review context YAML)\n\n### E1: SmolVLA VTR M-sweep (3-seed)\n- M=16 (87.5% compress): 56.9±1.3%, M=32: 60.1±1.3%, M=64: 62.0±2.3%, M=96: 54.5±3.2%, M=128 (passthrough): 58.0±3.5%\n- MLP-adapter@32: 63.4±2.6% (p=0.15 vs VTR cross-attention)\n- Baseline: 59.2%, Hard prune k=0.5: 0%\n- M-curve flat, architecture-independent re-encoding confirmed\n\n### E2: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector)\n- VTR M=128: 0% SR (overfitting). VTC-only M=32/64/96: all 0%.\n- OpenVLA baseline: 74%. Clean negative: VTR fails on MLP connectors.\n\n### E3: OpenVLA VTC M-sweep (M=32/64/96)\n- All M values: 0% SR. Training loss converges but doesn't transfer to closed-loop control.\n\n### E4: X-VLA cliff threshold (3-seed)\n- k=0.80: 89.0±0.72pp, k=0.85: 67.9±0.31pp. Non-monotonic, SD<1pp → deterministic.\n\n### E5: OFT CV measurement\n- OFT CV=0.219, OpenVLA CV=0.215. Delta=0.004. Action head doesn't affect pruning.\n\n### E6: Cross-suite 2-axis validation (5 models × 4 suites)\n- Framework accuracy 95%. X-VLA amplification Object→Goal: 27.4pp. π0.5 only 7.6pp.\n- Entangling connectors ≥27pp amplification, independent ≤10pp.\n\n### E7: VTR cross-suite generalization\n- Object: recovery ratio 1.015, Spatial: 1.21, Goal: 0.93, Long: 0.97 (predicted)\n\n### E8: π0.5 uniformly critical behavior\n- L2norm plateau (k≥0.85): Object 98%, Spatial 88.6%, Goal 88%, Long 78.4%\n- Random cliff: Object 74→28→9→5% at k=0.95→0.925→0.9→0.85\n- Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5: +36pp (Object), +16pp (Spatial), +13.8pp (Goal), -3.4pp (Long)\n\n### E9: Attention-based pruning (X-VLA)\n- Attn-last Object k=0.5: 99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → +56.6pp\n- Goal k=0.5: 98.2% (+39.2pp), Long k=0.5: 90.2% (+45.6pp)\n- At k=0.3: attn-mean 96.0% Object, 90.4% Spatial\n\n### E10: Scaling law\n- Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5: π0.5 +36, X-VLA +26.9, OpenVLA -1.8. |ρ|=1.0 Spearman at both k=0.5 and k=0.7.\n\n### E11: Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo)\n- CV≈0.22. Steep graded degradation. L2norm slightly better than random.\n- Baseline 58%, k=0.5: L2norm 10%, Random 8%.\n\n### E12: OFT graded degradation\n- Baseline ~97% Object. k=0.5 L2norm: 50%. Relative retention matches OpenVLA within 2pp.\n\n## Experiments NOT in Paper (from YAML)\n- VTR Long suite result (35.5% predicted, recovery ratio 0.97) — listed as predicted, may not be run\n- OFT full cross-suite pruning sweep — only partial results shown in paper\n- Perceiver Resampler results appear to be predicted/estimated rather than fully run\n\n## YOUR TASK\n\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Experimental Methodology**\n   - Is the experimental setup sound? Controls adequate?\n   - Are the evaluation metrics appropriate (SR on LIBERO)?\n   - Is the number of seeds sufficient? Statistical rigor?\n   - Any methodological gaps?\n\n2. **Results Analysis**\n   - Are claims well-supported by evidence?\n   - Any overclaimed results?\n   - Missing baselines or comparisons?\n   - Non-monotonic behaviors (π0.5 random, X-VLA cliff) — adequately explained?\n\n3. **VTR Method**\n   - Is the method well-motivated?\n   - Is the evaluation fair? Missing comparisons to other compression methods?\n   - 22M parameters + training cost — discussed adequately?\n\n4. **Reproducibility**\n   - Are implementation details sufficient?\n   - Can the experiments be reproduced?\n\n5. **Weaknesses**\n   - What are the main methodological weaknesses?\n   - Any concerns about cherry-picking or selective reporting?\n\nProvide scores for: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance. Then an overall score (1-10) with justification. List 3-5 main strengths and 3-5 main weaknesses. Format as a structured review."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPBhBkhNpoJAnoeFT78ayv","session_id":"eee2ebdf-357f-4a4d-85c6-2bc7a2b292e5","uuid":"c9f4fbb4-c86c-4852-a8b3-80c96397fc70","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:59:17.000Z"}
